WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.834
Wow! (running) 100 miles.

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:03.336
It looks like impossible, but not.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.005
because of course it'll be hard,

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.173
but if you know why you are here,

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.758
if it's a dream,

00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:10.260
I'm sure it's possible to do.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:53.506
- Good.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.466
Well, thank you for doing this.

00:02:55.466 --> 00:02:56.634
It's so nice to meet you.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:59.012
I can't wait to learn about your life.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.763
I'm excited to talk to you.

00:03:00.763 --> 00:03:04.309
And here we are in a running store

00:03:04.309 --> 00:03:05.852
in Boulder, Colorado,

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:08.897
doing this podcast,
Old School On the Road.

00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:12.150
And yeah, how are you doing today?

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:12.984
How are you feeling?

00:03:12.984 --> 00:03:15.820
How are you getting your head straight

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.489
for the big Hardrock 100?

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:19.699
- Yes.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:20.825
All of that.

00:03:20.825 --> 00:03:21.659
(man chuckling)

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:23.036
I'm so, so happy to be there

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.663
to make it to the US again.

00:03:25.663 --> 00:03:28.791
And I really enjoy this part of the season

00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:29.959
and the year,

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:32.170
and since yes, two years.

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:36.966
I'm so happy to build my season until June

00:03:36.966 --> 00:03:38.760
where I moved to Colorado,

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.430
and yeah, this year will
be special for sure too.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.184
And already today because I'm
so happy to discuss with you.

00:03:46.184 --> 00:03:49.896
I follow a bit your life,

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.231
and your different podcast,

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.191
and it's always interesting to have,

00:03:53.191 --> 00:03:56.945
yeah, this kind of a
different approach of running,

00:03:56.945 --> 00:04:00.907
and it's amazing to be
here to discuss with you.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.116
- I appreciate that.

00:04:02.116 --> 00:04:05.161
And you know, and kind of
reflecting on your life

00:04:05.161 --> 00:04:07.538
and your career,

00:04:07.538 --> 00:04:10.792
obviously you're one of
the greatest of all time

00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:12.669
in trail running.

00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:14.587
Four UTMB wins.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.798
You won Hardrock last year,

00:04:16.798 --> 00:04:17.715
set the record,

00:04:17.715 --> 00:04:19.926
you're going into Hardrock again,

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:23.596
coming up in a very short
period of time here.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:29.852
And my sense is that you're
very celebrated in Europe,

00:04:29.852 --> 00:04:33.064
but that in the United
States, or in North America,

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:34.023
perhaps less so.

00:04:34.023 --> 00:04:36.609
So I have a very specific
agenda for this podcast,

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:41.197
which is to help raise
awareness of your amazing talent

00:04:41.197 --> 00:04:42.824
and career.

00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:45.410
- Career, it's to be.
(man laughing)

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.619
- No, no.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.246
Well it's an interesting moment

00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:51.541
because I think that the
interest in trail running

00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:55.003
and adventure racing is
on the rise very much so.

00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:56.337
People are getting into it

00:04:56.337 --> 00:04:59.590
and it's just growing at an
explosive rate right now.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.593
And so I think that

00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:07.015
North America is very primed
to learn more about your life

00:05:07.015 --> 00:05:11.144
and how you've been able to
do the things that you do.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:15.064
- Yeah, I'm happy to discuss about that,

00:05:15.064 --> 00:05:17.567
but yeah, it's a bit party specific

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:19.235
because there's always,

00:05:20.111 --> 00:05:25.074
yes, a comparison between
Europe and North America,

00:05:25.408 --> 00:05:29.037
and everybody think in US and Europe,

00:05:29.037 --> 00:05:30.621
everybody think it's totally different.

00:05:30.621 --> 00:05:31.706
Trail running in US

00:05:31.706 --> 00:05:33.666
is totally different than
trail running in Europe,

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.335
or in France.

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:37.211
And for me, not at all.

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:41.049
We are just happy to be in the mountain

00:05:41.049 --> 00:05:44.594
and you have some very nice
and specific mountain here,

00:05:44.594 --> 00:05:46.387
and in France too, in Europe too.

00:05:46.387 --> 00:05:50.141
So for me it's just about being fascinated

00:05:50.141 --> 00:05:52.560
to spend some long day in the mountain

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.645
and to recenter about yourself,

00:05:54.645 --> 00:05:56.272
to try to, yeah,

00:05:56.272 --> 00:05:59.317
to to be the better part
of you in the mountain,

00:05:59.317 --> 00:06:00.610
and for some long day.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:04.364
So yeah, for me it's not
being American runner,

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:05.198
or being European runner.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.116
It's just being a mountain runner.

00:06:07.116 --> 00:06:11.454
And that's why I'm so happy to
discuss with American runner

00:06:11.454 --> 00:06:12.997
and to share my experience with them

00:06:12.997 --> 00:06:18.002
because it's always interesting
and funny to see a bit

00:06:18.169 --> 00:06:20.380
the media and how the people that can.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.214
- Right.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:22.465
- [Francois] Can discuss about that.

00:06:22.465 --> 00:06:25.635
- That that seems like maybe
that's an American thing.

00:06:25.635 --> 00:06:27.261
Like here in America we're thinking,

00:06:27.261 --> 00:06:29.263
oh, we have a certain way of training,

00:06:29.263 --> 00:06:31.140
but what are those guys over there doing?

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:31.974
In the Alps,

00:06:31.974 --> 00:06:33.267
they're living in small villages

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:35.186
and they're just going out

00:06:35.186 --> 00:06:38.272
way up into high elevation
every single day.

00:06:38.272 --> 00:06:39.732
And perhaps,

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:42.902
because we don't have access
to those types of mountains,

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:46.656
that there's something to your lifestyle

00:06:46.656 --> 00:06:49.951
or your kind of relationship with training

00:06:49.951 --> 00:06:51.202
that is very different

00:06:51.202 --> 00:06:53.496
than the way that the
Americans approach it.

00:06:53.496 --> 00:06:55.415
And I've heard you say like,

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:57.625
you kind of disabuse
people of this notion.

00:06:57.625 --> 00:06:59.877
You're like, no, it's not
actually that different.

00:06:59.877 --> 00:07:02.797
But your friend Jim Walmsley

00:07:02.797 --> 00:07:04.298
seems to be under that impression,

00:07:04.298 --> 00:07:06.008
which is why he moved to France.

00:07:06.008 --> 00:07:08.469
Feeling like that is
the missing ingredient

00:07:08.469 --> 00:07:11.848
in his ability to kind of win UTMB.

00:07:11.848 --> 00:07:14.684
He had to go and immerse
himself in that culture

00:07:14.684 --> 00:07:15.935
and that lifestyle.

00:07:16.853 --> 00:07:17.895
- We'll see,

00:07:17.895 --> 00:07:19.313
but no, I think,

00:07:20.314 --> 00:07:23.192
yeah, I think it could be
interesting to discuss with him,

00:07:23.192 --> 00:07:27.196
but I think it's not
just about the immersion

00:07:27.196 --> 00:07:28.781
in the French Alp

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.783
and French mountain made the difference.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:33.244
It's maybe more is the
approach of the event,

00:07:33.244 --> 00:07:35.204
more his approach of his training.

00:07:35.204 --> 00:07:38.624
And I'm sure he can do the
same training in the US

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:39.959
and I have the same approach

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:41.335
if it takes time for that.

00:07:41.335 --> 00:07:44.172
But I think in Flagstaff, it's very warm.

00:07:44.172 --> 00:07:47.133
It's a bit more flat than in France,

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:50.887
but I'm sure that in Silverton
he can train even better

00:07:50.887 --> 00:07:54.140
than in France for a race like UTMB.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:57.518
But it, for me, it's
very, very interesting.

00:07:57.518 --> 00:07:58.811
It's very nice to have a mountain

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:01.022
just like 200 meters from the house.

00:08:01.022 --> 00:08:03.483
So we can share some very
good training at the moment

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.318
and I really appreciate him.

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:08.112
But as a those American runner,

00:08:08.112 --> 00:08:11.532
it's always nice to, yes, to show culture,

00:08:11.532 --> 00:08:13.784
to share some very good moment.

00:08:13.784 --> 00:08:17.538
And yeah, I try to discover a bit more

00:08:17.538 --> 00:08:18.498
the US culture,

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:19.499
because I like it,

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:21.542
and they like European culture

00:08:21.542 --> 00:08:24.170
because I think it's something normal

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.255
that we are always more interesting

00:08:26.255 --> 00:08:30.551
about what is different from
what we are are used to.

00:08:30.551 --> 00:08:32.345
And for me it's very interesting

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:34.222
to discuss with American runner.

00:08:34.222 --> 00:08:37.225
I was there I think
the first time in 2012,

00:08:37.225 --> 00:08:39.227
but since 10 years now,

00:08:39.227 --> 00:08:43.147
I'm always, always so
happy to came back in US

00:08:43.147 --> 00:08:45.274
because I always learned
some different thing.

00:08:45.274 --> 00:08:49.737
And I'm always impressed
about how big this country

00:08:49.737 --> 00:08:50.571
and everything,
(man chuckling)

00:08:50.571 --> 00:08:52.490
and try them.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:54.116
In Europe and France,

00:08:54.116 --> 00:08:55.993
some of the longest rides,

00:08:55.993 --> 00:08:57.703
it's 100 miles,

00:08:57.703 --> 00:08:59.705
and I was, like four years ago,

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:01.624
the beginning of the Pacific Quest ride,

00:09:01.624 --> 00:09:04.752
It's 4,500 kids.
- Right.

00:09:04.752 --> 00:09:07.421
- Just unbelievable.

00:09:07.421 --> 00:09:10.216
So for me, it's amazing to be there.

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:12.009
- Yeah, I think,

00:09:12.009 --> 00:09:13.844
correct me if I'm wrong,

00:09:13.844 --> 00:09:17.598
the sense is that in the United States,

00:09:17.598 --> 00:09:20.643
people who are trying to
train at a certain level

00:09:21.852 --> 00:09:23.354
kind of complicate things

00:09:23.354 --> 00:09:26.399
or get really into data and spreadsheets

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:28.609
and get very much up in their head

00:09:28.609 --> 00:09:30.987
about how to approach these races.

00:09:30.987 --> 00:09:34.031
Whereas a European sensibility

00:09:34.031 --> 00:09:36.242
is more like we live in
these small villages,

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:37.076
we keep our,

00:09:37.076 --> 00:09:41.205
our lives are very kind of
less complex in that regard,

00:09:41.205 --> 00:09:44.083
and we keep things like
kind of very basic,

00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:48.754
and you know, I do feel
like there's some shared DNA

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:51.132
with somebody like Killian

00:09:51.132 --> 00:09:52.717
who will tell you

00:09:52.717 --> 00:09:54.677
it's just about your
relationship with nature,

00:09:54.677 --> 00:09:56.137
and it's about being outdoors,

00:09:56.137 --> 00:09:57.722
and the humility,

00:09:57.722 --> 00:10:00.516
and the experience of pushing your body

00:10:00.516 --> 00:10:04.687
and just being alone with
the majesty of the mountains,

00:10:04.687 --> 00:10:08.399
which is a different relationship
I think to performance

00:10:08.399 --> 00:10:10.776
than the kind of American mindset.

00:10:11.861 --> 00:10:12.695
- Yeah.

00:10:12.695 --> 00:10:14.322
Yeah, you're right I think.

00:10:14.322 --> 00:10:16.490
But it's, yeah.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:19.910
Yes, another are open, I like that.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:21.579
Not American, I like that too.

00:10:21.579 --> 00:10:24.749
But I think it's more
about a neutral approach,

00:10:24.749 --> 00:10:27.335
because I think when
it's more short distance,

00:10:27.335 --> 00:10:29.712
it could be totally different.

00:10:29.712 --> 00:10:30.880
But a neutral distance,

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.798
the approach I think must be different.

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:35.217
And I cannot speak for Killian,

00:10:35.217 --> 00:10:37.720
but I think it's a bit same as me.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.514
It's not that we, okay, we
want to be a top runner,

00:10:40.514 --> 00:10:41.599
a new, try mountain

00:10:41.599 --> 00:10:43.809
and so we have to do that now.

00:10:45.061 --> 00:10:46.520
We did that,

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:47.563
and because of that

00:10:47.563 --> 00:10:50.358
maybe we became some good, ultra runner,

00:10:50.358 --> 00:10:52.276
but it's totally different.

00:10:52.276 --> 00:10:54.070
But I want to became a good trail runner,

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:55.446
so I have to do that.

00:10:55.446 --> 00:10:58.282
Just say, anyway, I do that,

00:10:58.282 --> 00:11:00.660
so maybe I can became a
good trail runner or not.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:01.494
But anyway,

00:11:01.494 --> 00:11:03.829
we want to spend some
long days in the mountain.

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:04.997
We want to be there.

00:11:04.997 --> 00:11:06.415
We want to train like that.

00:11:06.415 --> 00:11:08.793
We want to have this kind of life,

00:11:08.793 --> 00:11:12.463
and just, I think the performance

00:11:15.591 --> 00:11:18.761
is just a consequence of our life.

00:11:18.761 --> 00:11:23.057
And I can think that's the
approach of some American runner

00:11:23.057 --> 00:11:23.891
is maybe a bit different.

00:11:23.891 --> 00:11:27.269
Oh, I would like to win
new UMTB maybe one day

00:11:27.269 --> 00:11:28.104
or something that,

00:11:28.104 --> 00:11:29.355
so I have to train like that.

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:30.356
I have to do that.

00:11:30.356 --> 00:11:31.190
I have to do that.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:34.485
And it's not, I think, the same way.

00:11:35.319 --> 00:11:37.238
The beginning must be okay,

00:11:37.238 --> 00:11:38.114
I'd like,

00:11:38.114 --> 00:11:40.157
I would like to be in the mountain.

00:11:40.157 --> 00:11:41.826
I would like to experience myself.

00:11:41.826 --> 00:11:43.452
I would like to push my limits

00:11:43.452 --> 00:11:44.995
to discover that kind of trail,

00:11:44.995 --> 00:11:46.956
that kind of mountain.

00:11:46.956 --> 00:11:48.666
And then the consequence would be that,

00:11:48.666 --> 00:11:49.959
ah, because of that life,

00:11:49.959 --> 00:11:51.210
because of that training,

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.504
you will be, sure, in front of the scene.

00:11:53.504 --> 00:11:55.005
And for short distance,

00:11:55.005 --> 00:11:56.716
I think it's not the same thing.

00:11:56.716 --> 00:11:59.301
Okay, I want to be a
performer on short distance.

00:11:59.301 --> 00:12:01.220
You go do training, whatever you want.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:03.431
Okay, so I have to focus on my training.

00:12:03.431 --> 00:12:04.682
I have to be professional.

00:12:04.682 --> 00:12:06.225
I have to do that, that, that,

00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:07.768
and then you have a result.

00:12:07.768 --> 00:12:09.019
But on the trail,

00:12:09.019 --> 00:12:10.354
I think it's too many things.

00:12:10.354 --> 00:12:11.564
It's okay, it's the training,

00:12:11.564 --> 00:12:12.398
it's the performance,

00:12:12.398 --> 00:12:13.607
it's your body,

00:12:13.607 --> 00:12:16.652
but first, it's a mentality.

00:12:16.652 --> 00:12:17.528
It's a approach.

00:12:17.528 --> 00:12:18.696
It's how we train.

00:12:18.696 --> 00:12:20.156
And I know,

00:12:21.073 --> 00:12:23.576
I know well I think Colton Walter,

00:12:23.576 --> 00:12:25.119
you made you some post.
- Yeah.

00:12:25.119 --> 00:12:28.330
- And I think she's one of those

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:30.583
who have this kind of approach.

00:12:30.583 --> 00:12:32.001
She don't take care about the result,

00:12:32.001 --> 00:12:33.335
the race, or everything.

00:12:33.335 --> 00:12:35.421
What she like is to be out,

00:12:35.421 --> 00:12:37.256
out in the mountain,

00:12:37.256 --> 00:12:38.966
to spend some long day.

00:12:38.966 --> 00:12:42.428
And then if she can win
a race, she's happy.

00:12:42.428 --> 00:12:43.846
And finally is a result,

00:12:43.846 --> 00:12:47.349
is just the consequence of what
she did all along the year.

00:12:47.349 --> 00:12:50.311
She don't focus on one
race or another race.

00:12:50.311 --> 00:12:51.729
If it's not working on one race,

00:12:51.729 --> 00:12:52.855
okay, no work.

00:12:52.855 --> 00:12:53.856
It's not good.

00:12:53.856 --> 00:12:54.690
But no worry.

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:56.525
She have a another race or another plan,

00:12:56.525 --> 00:12:59.653
and anyway, she's so
happy to train for that.

00:12:59.653 --> 00:13:00.946
So it's not the same approach.

00:13:00.946 --> 00:13:04.241
And I try to discuss a
lot with Jim about that

00:13:04.241 --> 00:13:06.160
because if he's approach is,

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.329
okay, I would like to be
the first American runner

00:13:08.329 --> 00:13:10.331
to win UTMB.

00:13:11.332 --> 00:13:13.501
The pressure is really high.

00:13:13.501 --> 00:13:15.461
I hope he will able to do that

00:13:15.461 --> 00:13:17.797
because he's an amazing runner.

00:13:17.797 --> 00:13:19.757
He's very, very good.

00:13:19.757 --> 00:13:22.635
But the approach is, it's hard for me.

00:13:22.635 --> 00:13:25.471
I think if I have that kind of approach,

00:13:25.471 --> 00:13:27.932
it's impossible for me to win a race.

00:13:27.932 --> 00:13:28.808
- Right, right, right.

00:13:28.808 --> 00:13:31.477
So essentially what you're saying is

00:13:31.477 --> 00:13:32.895
in the long run,

00:13:32.895 --> 00:13:36.482
especially with these longer
distance mountain races,

00:13:39.401 --> 00:13:41.362
achieving goals

00:13:41.362 --> 00:13:44.698
only comes as a consequence

00:13:44.698 --> 00:13:47.034
of the lifestyle that you live,

00:13:47.034 --> 00:13:49.537
as opposed to being very
kind of driven towards

00:13:49.537 --> 00:13:50.830
a specific result.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:52.248
And I've heard you say,

00:13:53.666 --> 00:13:55.167
I think it was with respect to,

00:13:55.167 --> 00:13:58.295
maybe it was UTMB last year,

00:13:58.295 --> 00:13:59.255
the question was like,

00:13:59.255 --> 00:14:03.133
how do you shoulder the
pressure of going into UTMB?

00:14:03.133 --> 00:14:04.176
You've won three times.

00:14:04.176 --> 00:14:05.261
Can you do it again?

00:14:06.262 --> 00:14:07.721
That must be overwhelming.

00:14:07.721 --> 00:14:08.639
And you said something like,

00:14:08.639 --> 00:14:10.683
"Well, if I win, great.

00:14:10.683 --> 00:14:12.560
But if I don't, I'll take my kids

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.478
to go do something,

00:14:14.478 --> 00:14:16.522
and I have a whole life outside of this."

00:14:16.522 --> 00:14:18.732
And that was what kind of made me think

00:14:18.732 --> 00:14:20.985
of the difference in sensibility

00:14:20.985 --> 00:14:24.446
of kind of a European mindset
versus an American mindset.

00:14:24.446 --> 00:14:27.157
Whereas the American would
be devastated if they lost

00:14:27.157 --> 00:14:29.535
and they're clenching their fists,

00:14:29.535 --> 00:14:31.328
and you know, trying to drive,

00:14:31.328 --> 00:14:33.372
kind of will a certain result as,

00:14:33.372 --> 00:14:37.668
so it's like the difference
between self will

00:14:37.668 --> 00:14:40.880
versus being in the allowing, right?

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:42.756
Like if I'm living my lifestyle,

00:14:42.756 --> 00:14:45.926
I'm allowing the result to unfold

00:14:45.926 --> 00:14:48.846
that is meant to be as a
result of the decisions

00:14:48.846 --> 00:14:50.723
that I've made about how I live my life.

00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:52.349
- Yeah, it's true.

00:14:52.349 --> 00:14:54.768
It's even more easy for me to say that

00:14:54.768 --> 00:14:56.270
when you won it three times.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:57.396
(man laughing)

00:14:57.396 --> 00:14:58.230
- Right.

00:14:58.230 --> 00:14:59.773
- Okay, you don't have pressure,

00:14:59.773 --> 00:15:00.774
but you won it three times.

00:15:00.774 --> 00:15:02.109
So it's easy to say that.

00:15:02.109 --> 00:15:02.943
Okay, sure.

00:15:02.943 --> 00:15:04.069
But for me, even the first time,

00:15:04.069 --> 00:15:06.488
if I arrive at the start line
with this kind of pressure,

00:15:06.488 --> 00:15:09.825
I'm sure I won't able to finish,

00:15:09.825 --> 00:15:12.328
because I want to protect myself,

00:15:12.328 --> 00:15:13.871
and at the start line

00:15:13.871 --> 00:15:15.497
I don't want to have
this kind of pressure.

00:15:15.497 --> 00:15:16.999
So I'm at the start line.

00:15:16.999 --> 00:15:19.376
I say, okay, I have a very good training.

00:15:19.376 --> 00:15:21.378
I have some two very good months

00:15:21.378 --> 00:15:23.923
and I'm so happy to be there.

00:15:23.923 --> 00:15:26.383
If I can win, if I can finish two,

00:15:26.383 --> 00:15:27.593
on the podium, whatever,

00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:29.929
it's so, so good.

00:15:29.929 --> 00:15:32.097
So I will be so happy.

00:15:32.097 --> 00:15:34.058
But if not,

00:15:34.058 --> 00:15:35.017
it's okay.

00:15:35.017 --> 00:15:35.851
It's just a sport.

00:15:35.851 --> 00:15:36.977
It's just a pleasure.
- [Rich] Right.

00:15:36.977 --> 00:15:38.270
- And my life will continue,

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.897
and I will have some possibility,

00:15:39.897 --> 00:15:40.981
and some other chance.

00:15:40.981 --> 00:15:43.692
But for me, it's taken like 20 years maybe

00:15:43.692 --> 00:15:46.904
to arrive at the start
line with this position

00:15:46.904 --> 00:15:48.405
and without any pressure,

00:15:48.405 --> 00:15:50.783
and it's not easy every day.

00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:52.451
Every day you have to work on yourself

00:15:52.451 --> 00:15:53.410
and to say it again.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:55.454
And that's why I don't want to go back

00:15:55.454 --> 00:15:57.289
each year on the same race.

00:15:57.289 --> 00:15:59.083
Like for me this year,

00:15:59.083 --> 00:16:01.835
going back to a Hardrock 100 again,

00:16:01.835 --> 00:16:04.213
just one year after
where you finish first,

00:16:04.213 --> 00:16:05.714
when you break the record.

00:16:05.714 --> 00:16:07.091
I was not expected that.

00:16:07.091 --> 00:16:08.258
Last year I was thinking, okay,

00:16:08.258 --> 00:16:09.885
it's just an experience for me.

00:16:09.885 --> 00:16:12.763
Next year I will come back
and I will do it better,

00:16:12.763 --> 00:16:14.682
but last year I finished,

00:16:14.682 --> 00:16:16.684
I say, how can I do it better?

00:16:16.684 --> 00:16:19.395
So this year, you came
back with a bit of pressure

00:16:19.395 --> 00:16:20.646
because even for yourself,

00:16:20.646 --> 00:16:21.480
you cannot say, okay,

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:24.024
I will be there just to try to finish.

00:16:24.024 --> 00:16:24.858
Come on.

00:16:24.858 --> 00:16:25.693
Last year you win,

00:16:25.693 --> 00:16:26.610
you break the record,

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:28.821
you got no just here to finish.

00:16:28.821 --> 00:16:29.613
(man laughing)

00:16:29.613 --> 00:16:30.656
So for me this year,

00:16:30.656 --> 00:16:31.865
it's a bit more pressure,

00:16:31.865 --> 00:16:36.245
but that's why I try to
have a another approach

00:16:36.245 --> 00:16:38.330
to say, okay, I'm here.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:39.915
Last year, it was just incredible.

00:16:39.915 --> 00:16:40.749
I was lucky.

00:16:40.749 --> 00:16:41.709
So I'm I again,

00:16:41.709 --> 00:16:43.836
so it's so good.

00:16:43.836 --> 00:16:44.795
I'm so lucky too.

00:16:44.795 --> 00:16:46.380
So it's another race,

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.506
it's another race.

00:16:47.506 --> 00:16:48.966
There's some another runner.

00:16:48.966 --> 00:16:50.259
So yes, I will,

00:16:50.259 --> 00:16:53.178
I would like just to finish it

00:16:53.178 --> 00:16:55.264
and to it just,

00:16:55.264 --> 00:16:58.183
yeah, we are just 160
runners at the start line,

00:16:58.183 --> 00:17:00.978
so I'm so lucky to be there.

00:17:00.978 --> 00:17:04.690
Just a huge community of
ultra trail runner in the US.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:06.650
It's just like a family.

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:09.528
Everybody are so happy to meet each other.

00:17:09.528 --> 00:17:11.113
Like even tonight in Boulder,

00:17:11.113 --> 00:17:13.323
I think it will be so nice to have a,

00:17:13.323 --> 00:17:14.700
like a common event,

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:18.162
and for me I say, okay, please enjoy it

00:17:18.162 --> 00:17:20.289
and don't push your pressure on yourself.

00:17:20.289 --> 00:17:21.457
And with that way,

00:17:21.457 --> 00:17:23.500
I'm sure the race would be good.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:24.334
- Right.

00:17:24.334 --> 00:17:26.754
It's such a healthy strategy,

00:17:26.754 --> 00:17:30.424
and one that has longevity to it, right?

00:17:30.424 --> 00:17:35.054
Because you're releasing yourself
from carrying that burden.

00:17:35.054 --> 00:17:37.931
It's confidence in the preparation,

00:17:37.931 --> 00:17:40.225
gratitude for just being able to be there

00:17:40.225 --> 00:17:42.102
and be healthy and participate,

00:17:42.102 --> 00:17:44.396
and also kind of a healthy respect

00:17:44.396 --> 00:17:47.483
for all the variables
that you don't control;

00:17:47.483 --> 00:17:49.151
the weather, and other people,

00:17:49.151 --> 00:17:50.402
and all that kind of stuff, right?

00:17:50.402 --> 00:17:51.904
Like, the longer the race,

00:17:51.904 --> 00:17:53.572
the less control you actually have.

00:17:53.572 --> 00:17:57.785
You just have the
preparation that you endured

00:17:57.785 --> 00:17:58.744
just to get there.

00:17:58.744 --> 00:18:03.749
And I was listening to your
conversation with Dylan Bowman.

00:18:04.792 --> 00:18:06.877
You guys were talking
about Hardrock last year

00:18:06.877 --> 00:18:08.587
and how you were,

00:18:08.587 --> 00:18:11.423
you were kind of running near each other,

00:18:11.423 --> 00:18:14.051
and realizing that you were like way ahead

00:18:14.051 --> 00:18:16.386
the record that Killian had set

00:18:16.386 --> 00:18:20.015
and thinking maybe perhaps
we've made a terrible error.

00:18:20.015 --> 00:18:22.643
- Yeah, exactly.
(men laughing)

00:18:22.643 --> 00:18:23.977
- And it all worked out.

00:18:23.977 --> 00:18:26.772
But then thinking, well how
can I do better this year?

00:18:26.772 --> 00:18:29.233
And saying, well, maybe I
don't have to worry about that.

00:18:29.233 --> 00:18:32.528
I'm just here to experience the community,

00:18:32.528 --> 00:18:35.322
and to do my best.

00:18:35.322 --> 00:18:38.492
And I think the community piece
is also really interesting.

00:18:38.492 --> 00:18:43.455
I know that last year was
the first running of Hardrock

00:18:43.455 --> 00:18:45.249
in three years because of COVID,

00:18:45.249 --> 00:18:48.919
and also weather conditions prior to that.

00:18:48.919 --> 00:18:52.631
But you had come to
Silverton in 2019 nonetheless

00:18:52.631 --> 00:18:55.259
to engage with the community,

00:18:55.259 --> 00:18:57.010
train on the course,

00:18:57.010 --> 00:18:58.095
and kind of,

00:18:58.095 --> 00:19:01.682
now you've become kind
of part of that community

00:19:01.682 --> 00:19:03.934
that you're returning to tomorrow.

00:19:03.934 --> 00:19:05.310
- Yeah, exactly.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:09.523
It was very nice in 2019
to be able to be there,

00:19:09.523 --> 00:19:11.608
and we have some very good moments,

00:19:11.608 --> 00:19:14.736
and we discover the race
without any pressure

00:19:14.736 --> 00:19:15.779
with each other.

00:19:15.779 --> 00:19:17.447
It was very, very interesting.

00:19:17.447 --> 00:19:18.490
There's a lot of snow,

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:21.118
so it was very interesting
to play in the snow

00:19:21.118 --> 00:19:22.953
because people like Jim,

00:19:22.953 --> 00:19:26.623
they just learned how to run
on the snow four years ago.

00:19:26.623 --> 00:19:28.333
So it was very interesting for me

00:19:28.333 --> 00:19:30.711
to discuss about that with them.

00:19:30.711 --> 00:19:31.837
And yes,

00:19:32.796 --> 00:19:35.591
it would be very interesting

00:19:35.591 --> 00:19:40.179
and it's not a good thing that
Dylan won't race this year

00:19:40.179 --> 00:19:42.764
because here we are an incredible day.

00:19:42.764 --> 00:19:46.476
So even for him, I think
he was not expecting

00:19:46.476 --> 00:19:49.104
to run so fast at that basin.

00:19:49.104 --> 00:19:51.064
Yes, during all the race we are thinking,

00:19:51.064 --> 00:19:52.816
oh, maybe we're out too fast.

00:19:52.816 --> 00:19:56.028
Anyway, we have a very
good day so we continue.

00:19:56.028 --> 00:19:56.862
(man laughing)

00:19:56.862 --> 00:19:58.989
- Do you think about
the other competitors?

00:19:58.989 --> 00:20:01.033
I texted Dylan yesterday

00:20:01.033 --> 00:20:03.702
and I said I'm gonna
be talking to Francois.

00:20:03.702 --> 00:20:08.081
What would be interesting
for me to explore with him

00:20:08.081 --> 00:20:11.335
that is something I can't
Google or find out online?

00:20:11.335 --> 00:20:12.169
And he's like,

00:20:12.169 --> 00:20:15.088
"I'm so fascinated by
Francois's relationship

00:20:15.088 --> 00:20:16.715
with competition."

00:20:16.715 --> 00:20:18.884
And we've already kind
of covered a little bit

00:20:18.884 --> 00:20:21.345
of your sensibility with that,

00:20:21.345 --> 00:20:23.722
but you seem so,

00:20:23.722 --> 00:20:27.100
it's really not about like what
anyone else is doing, right?

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:28.977
Like, the longer the race is,

00:20:28.977 --> 00:20:31.605
the less it is about some other performer.

00:20:31.605 --> 00:20:35.901
It's just about your relationship
with you and the terrain.

00:20:35.901 --> 00:20:36.818
- Yeah, yeah.

00:20:36.818 --> 00:20:38.445
It's exactly that.

00:20:38.445 --> 00:20:41.448
I don't take care about those runner

00:20:41.448 --> 00:20:43.492
even before the race,

00:20:43.492 --> 00:20:45.327
even normally during the race,

00:20:45.327 --> 00:20:47.579
but I'm a bit too competitor.

00:20:47.579 --> 00:20:49.206
So when I'm doing the race,

00:20:49.206 --> 00:20:52.251
I really like and enjoy to
play with those other runner,

00:20:52.251 --> 00:20:54.920
but it's not my main goal for sure.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:56.046
- Do you think about,

00:20:56.046 --> 00:20:58.757
oh, I know this runner uses this strategy

00:20:58.757 --> 00:21:00.217
so I have to look out for that,

00:21:00.217 --> 00:21:01.718
or do you not pay
attention to any of that?

00:21:01.718 --> 00:21:03.095
- No, I know that,

00:21:03.095 --> 00:21:04.304
and I play with that,

00:21:04.304 --> 00:21:07.432
and I, yeah, you have time
to think during 24 hours,

00:21:07.432 --> 00:21:08.642
so you can think,

00:21:08.642 --> 00:21:09.893
okay, maybe this runner is going too fast

00:21:09.893 --> 00:21:11.144
because I know him,

00:21:11.144 --> 00:21:13.272
so I don't have to take care about that.

00:21:13.272 --> 00:21:14.439
But you play with that.

00:21:14.439 --> 00:21:16.358
But you have to,

00:21:16.358 --> 00:21:18.944
your main focus must be on you,

00:21:18.944 --> 00:21:21.113
otherwise I think it's too hard on you,

00:21:21.113 --> 00:21:23.699
and that's why I really
like ultra trail running.

00:21:23.699 --> 00:21:26.493
It's totally different
from the other distance.

00:21:26.493 --> 00:21:29.079
I think even since 100K an hour,

00:21:29.079 --> 00:21:30.580
and even more,

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.875
I think less than like
Western States time,

00:21:33.875 --> 00:21:35.460
it's 40 minutes.

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:38.046
It's around like 14 hour I think.

00:21:38.046 --> 00:21:39.172
- [Rich] Yeah.
- I think

00:21:39.172 --> 00:21:40.757
more than 14 an hour.

00:21:40.757 --> 00:21:41.675
It's another world.

00:21:41.675 --> 00:21:42.801
- Right.

00:21:42.801 --> 00:21:43.969
- So less than 14 hour,

00:21:43.969 --> 00:21:46.054
I think now competitors are,

00:21:46.054 --> 00:21:47.681
yes, well experienced.

00:21:47.681 --> 00:21:48.557
They are training for that.

00:21:48.557 --> 00:21:52.144
They are very conditioning for that,

00:21:52.144 --> 00:21:54.396
so I think less than 14 hours,

00:21:54.396 --> 00:21:56.982
it's more like athletics and race.

00:21:56.982 --> 00:21:59.192
More than 14, 16 hour,

00:21:59.192 --> 00:22:00.861
I think it's another world,

00:22:00.861 --> 00:22:02.696
and more than 20 hour,

00:22:02.696 --> 00:22:05.490
it's, again, something else.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:08.785
So I think it's very important
to have a different approach

00:22:08.785 --> 00:22:11.413
and that's why I think I'm still there

00:22:11.413 --> 00:22:12.247
after like,

00:22:13.248 --> 00:22:16.418
my first long distance was 2006, I think.

00:22:16.418 --> 00:22:17.627
So it's 12 years ago

00:22:17.627 --> 00:22:20.797
and normally you cannot
make it such long career

00:22:20.797 --> 00:22:23.592
in high performance in sport.

00:22:23.592 --> 00:22:26.762
- Right.
- But if I'm still there,

00:22:26.762 --> 00:22:29.931
it's maybe because this is
the spot totally different

00:22:29.931 --> 00:22:32.059
and where experience helps you a lot

00:22:33.643 --> 00:22:34.895
and approach helps you a lot,

00:22:34.895 --> 00:22:38.857
and yes, that's why I think
I still continue to progress

00:22:38.857 --> 00:22:41.860
even if now I'm maybe too old for that.

00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:42.694
- Yeah, no, no, no.

00:22:42.694 --> 00:22:43.862
- But I really enjoy that,

00:22:43.862 --> 00:22:45.155
and I think we experience,

00:22:45.155 --> 00:22:49.117
it's something just interesting in Utah.

00:22:49.117 --> 00:22:51.578
- Yeah, I mean there is a long history

00:22:51.578 --> 00:22:53.080
in ultra running

00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:55.290
where somebody will burst onto the scene

00:22:55.290 --> 00:22:57.459
and they'll have unbelievable performances

00:22:57.459 --> 00:23:00.045
for maybe two years, three years,

00:23:00.045 --> 00:23:03.131
and then whether it's
over training, or burnout,

00:23:03.131 --> 00:23:04.091
or whatever it is,

00:23:04.091 --> 00:23:07.636
they're unable to ever kind
of match that level again.

00:23:07.636 --> 00:23:10.138
You don't see very many people

00:23:10.138 --> 00:23:12.432
who have longevity in their careers.

00:23:12.432 --> 00:23:14.351
- Yeah, it's so sad for me,

00:23:14.351 --> 00:23:16.895
and that's why I have
this kind of approach

00:23:16.895 --> 00:23:19.272
and I try to push that kind
of approach for the media

00:23:19.272 --> 00:23:22.943
because I'm so sad when I
see some runner just say,

00:23:22.943 --> 00:23:25.904
okay, I will try to do six
or seven trail run in a year

00:23:25.904 --> 00:23:27.322
or even four in a year.

00:23:27.322 --> 00:23:30.033
Even in France, they have
some amazing runners.

00:23:30.033 --> 00:23:30.867
They say, okay,

00:23:30.867 --> 00:23:32.452
we like to do like UTMB,

00:23:32.452 --> 00:23:33.495
and Diagonale des Fous,

00:23:33.495 --> 00:23:34.496
and some other race,

00:23:34.496 --> 00:23:36.039
and now it's,

00:23:36.039 --> 00:23:37.541
I think it's too much.

00:23:37.541 --> 00:23:38.708
Maybe it could be one year.

00:23:38.708 --> 00:23:41.878
Like last year I tried
to running back to back

00:23:41.878 --> 00:23:43.797
Hardrock and UTMB.

00:23:43.797 --> 00:23:44.798
It's only six weeks,

00:23:44.798 --> 00:23:48.385
but it was my only goal for the year

00:23:48.385 --> 00:23:50.637
and I propose that once since three years,

00:23:50.637 --> 00:23:53.014
and I run since 25 years.

00:23:53.014 --> 00:23:55.809
So it's not just, okay,
you do it last year,

00:23:55.809 --> 00:23:57.144
Next year you can do now.

00:23:57.144 --> 00:23:58.645
No, it's something very special

00:23:58.645 --> 00:24:00.730
and I won't do it again this year.

00:24:00.730 --> 00:24:02.524
And I think for Killian,

00:24:02.524 --> 00:24:04.025
he will try to do it this year

00:24:04.025 --> 00:24:05.944
and even at the middle,

00:24:05.944 --> 00:24:07.487
but it's Killian.

00:24:07.487 --> 00:24:09.906
He runs since he was born.

00:24:09.906 --> 00:24:12.451
- [Rich] Yeah.
- So it's not everybody

00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:13.285
can do that,

00:24:13.285 --> 00:24:15.745
because you mustn't do that I think.

00:24:16.663 --> 00:24:21.585
Stop Martin, they did two race in a year

00:24:21.585 --> 00:24:23.420
and it's two hour,

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:25.088
and for us, it's 24 hours,

00:24:25.088 --> 00:24:27.048
so how can we do more than two race?

00:24:27.048 --> 00:24:28.175
- Right.
- And I see

00:24:28.175 --> 00:24:29.968
so many, many runner,

00:24:29.968 --> 00:24:33.847
even American runner when I
start in 2012 they were there,

00:24:33.847 --> 00:24:35.974
and now it's so hard for them.

00:24:35.974 --> 00:24:38.143
I think about like Rob Krause,

00:24:38.143 --> 00:24:39.227
or some people,

00:24:40.270 --> 00:24:41.980
Jeff Rose or some people like that.

00:24:41.980 --> 00:24:43.315
Even Anton, it's, yeah,

00:24:43.315 --> 00:24:44.858
there was a race,

00:24:44.858 --> 00:24:46.860
and maybe sometimes too much,

00:24:46.860 --> 00:24:48.737
and then it was too hard to recover

00:24:49.696 --> 00:24:50.822
and they were so good,

00:24:50.822 --> 00:24:53.325
and I think maybe they get over train

00:24:53.325 --> 00:24:56.411
or too much pressure
or something like that,

00:24:56.411 --> 00:24:59.414
and then it's too hard
for the body to come back.

00:24:59.414 --> 00:25:01.041
- [Rich] Right.
- So we have to be really,

00:25:01.041 --> 00:25:02.918
we relax about that,

00:25:02.918 --> 00:25:05.462
and we discuss a lot with Jim about that.

00:25:05.462 --> 00:25:09.174
And this year that's why
he did a race in April,

00:25:09.174 --> 00:25:10.467
and then he's okay.

00:25:10.467 --> 00:25:12.135
Now I just focus on UTMB

00:25:12.135 --> 00:25:14.429
and maybe it'll be my decision.

00:25:14.429 --> 00:25:16.473
I think ah, it's a very good approach

00:25:16.473 --> 00:25:17.307
and I like it

00:25:17.307 --> 00:25:19.601
because you will be very fresh,

00:25:19.601 --> 00:25:22.354
and I'm sure that next year
you will be there again.

00:25:22.354 --> 00:25:24.356
And this is the most important for me.

00:25:24.356 --> 00:25:25.815
Winning a race, it's important,

00:25:25.815 --> 00:25:29.027
but be able to run again in five years

00:25:29.027 --> 00:25:31.321
I think it's the most
important thing for us

00:25:31.321 --> 00:25:32.572
and for our body.

00:25:32.572 --> 00:25:33.740
- Yeah, sure.

00:25:33.740 --> 00:25:36.701
I mean I think that the sport is maturing

00:25:36.701 --> 00:25:40.205
in terms of how people
are understanding training

00:25:40.205 --> 00:25:41.706
and performance.

00:25:41.706 --> 00:25:43.792
Those runners that you mentioned,

00:25:43.792 --> 00:25:45.669
and even the generation prior to that,

00:25:45.669 --> 00:25:47.254
like very little was known

00:25:47.254 --> 00:25:49.130
'cause people were pushing the boundaries

00:25:49.130 --> 00:25:52.050
of the distances that anybody thought

00:25:52.050 --> 00:25:54.135
humans could even run to begin with.

00:25:54.135 --> 00:25:55.929
And so of course the mentality was like,

00:25:55.929 --> 00:25:57.556
well if we can do that, let's train more,

00:25:57.556 --> 00:25:58.723
let's train more.

00:25:58.723 --> 00:26:00.600
And then suddenly all of these people

00:26:00.600 --> 00:26:02.769
are kind of falling off the wayside.

00:26:02.769 --> 00:26:04.980
But we saw Anton come back

00:26:04.980 --> 00:26:08.275
after that long period of absence.

00:26:08.275 --> 00:26:10.026
So I think there is that,

00:26:10.026 --> 00:26:11.194
now it's like,

00:26:11.194 --> 00:26:13.488
oh, well if you were one of those people

00:26:13.488 --> 00:26:16.658
maybe you can rebuild in
a new and different way.

00:26:16.658 --> 00:26:19.619
- Yeah, it was so nice to see him again,

00:26:19.619 --> 00:26:21.913
and I chat with him yesterday

00:26:21.913 --> 00:26:24.457
because I know that he
lived not so far from there

00:26:24.457 --> 00:26:26.793
and he is a bit focused on bicycle.

00:26:26.793 --> 00:26:29.754
- Yeah, he's out on Instagram
riding his bike everywhere.

00:26:29.754 --> 00:26:32.340
- He will do 600 miles on Friday.

00:26:32.340 --> 00:26:34.718
(men laughing)

00:26:34.718 --> 00:26:36.219
Okay.

00:26:36.219 --> 00:26:39.055
But yeah, it was so nice to see him again,

00:26:39.055 --> 00:26:40.682
and yeah, and Anton,

00:26:40.682 --> 00:26:45.353
Joe Grant, I'm sure I will see
him in Hardrock in two days.

00:26:45.353 --> 00:26:47.981
It's so nice to continue
to discuss with them.

00:26:47.981 --> 00:26:51.568
Every year I'm so happy
to meet Anna Frost,

00:26:51.568 --> 00:26:53.486
and she was here even before me

00:26:53.486 --> 00:26:55.655
in the trail running community,

00:26:55.655 --> 00:26:59.117
and it's so nice to see
that that kind of people.

00:26:59.117 --> 00:27:01.911
Okay, they're so happy
about their performance,

00:27:01.911 --> 00:27:03.663
and about their career,

00:27:03.663 --> 00:27:06.374
and which race that they was able to win,

00:27:06.374 --> 00:27:09.628
but they are even more
happy to be still there

00:27:09.628 --> 00:27:11.254
and still able to run.

00:27:11.254 --> 00:27:13.506
And if you discuss with them,

00:27:13.506 --> 00:27:16.092
they will, I'm sure
100% that they would say

00:27:16.092 --> 00:27:18.219
it's the most important thing

00:27:18.219 --> 00:27:21.473
is just be able to be
again in the mountain today

00:27:21.473 --> 00:27:23.308
to be able to have some long day

00:27:23.308 --> 00:27:25.644
and to share some nice one with
the people in the community.

00:27:25.644 --> 00:27:28.146
It's even more important
than winning that race,

00:27:28.146 --> 00:27:28.980
other race,

00:27:28.980 --> 00:27:31.900
or pushing too much for that,

00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:36.196
because in 20 years,
what will you remember?

00:27:36.196 --> 00:27:39.032
Oh, I was able to do
that, but now I'm not.

00:27:39.032 --> 00:27:40.367
I don't want to run anymore.

00:27:40.367 --> 00:27:42.619
I don't want to be in the mountain.

00:27:42.619 --> 00:27:43.453
- Right.
- I'm not

00:27:43.453 --> 00:27:44.621
passionate about that.

00:27:44.621 --> 00:27:45.914
Well, okay, I did that,

00:27:45.914 --> 00:27:47.415
but I'm still there,

00:27:47.415 --> 00:27:50.585
and I'm still so happy and
so passionate to do that.

00:27:50.585 --> 00:27:52.545
And for me it's the most
important thing that,

00:27:52.545 --> 00:27:54.422
okay.
- Remaining joyful

00:27:54.422 --> 00:27:57.884
about the whole experience.
- I just want to be there

00:27:57.884 --> 00:28:00.011
in five or 10 years with my kids

00:28:00.011 --> 00:28:03.431
and to say, okay, I'm so happy
to share with you this loop

00:28:03.431 --> 00:28:04.265
around Mont Blanc,

00:28:04.265 --> 00:28:08.228
or, you know, kids, I
was there in Silverton

00:28:08.228 --> 00:28:09.562
like 20 years ago,

00:28:09.562 --> 00:28:11.314
and I now I'm still there with you

00:28:11.314 --> 00:28:12.816
and I'm able to make a loop.

00:28:12.816 --> 00:28:16.319
Ah, I think it's my biggest dream actually

00:28:16.319 --> 00:28:18.446
even more than winning again the race,

00:28:18.446 --> 00:28:20.281
is just too be there
in 10 years and to say,

00:28:20.281 --> 00:28:21.700
okay, I was there,

00:28:21.700 --> 00:28:22.909
and I can share it with you.

00:28:22.909 --> 00:28:23.993
It's, wow,

00:28:23.993 --> 00:28:26.162
this is for me the most important thing.

00:28:26.162 --> 00:28:27.247
- That's all fine.

00:28:27.247 --> 00:28:28.748
But come on, let's get honest here.

00:28:28.748 --> 00:28:30.125
I don't wanna make you uncomfortable,

00:28:30.125 --> 00:28:32.460
but like four UTMB wins.

00:28:32.460 --> 00:28:35.630
I mean, there's gotta be a
killer under the surface there.

00:28:35.630 --> 00:28:37.048
Like, what?

00:28:37.048 --> 00:28:39.676
Why are you so much
better than everyone else?

00:28:39.676 --> 00:28:41.386
(men laughing)

00:28:41.386 --> 00:28:43.763
What is the secret weapon?

00:28:43.763 --> 00:28:46.057
What are you doing that
others aren't doing?

00:28:46.057 --> 00:28:51.062
Or how are you built physiologically

00:28:51.646 --> 00:28:54.858
so that you are so
exceptional at this sport?

00:28:56.651 --> 00:28:58.361
- I don't know.
(man laughing)

00:28:58.361 --> 00:29:00.488
I'm so passionated

00:29:00.488 --> 00:29:03.700
when you are at the start line,

00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:07.245
if you build like, we speak earlier,

00:29:07.245 --> 00:29:08.538
when you are the start line,

00:29:08.538 --> 00:29:10.206
you just, you don't feel the pressure.

00:29:10.206 --> 00:29:13.084
You just feel the power just to say,

00:29:13.084 --> 00:29:14.294
wow, I'm here.

00:29:14.294 --> 00:29:16.755
I wait that moment since
two years and I'm here.

00:29:17.630 --> 00:29:22.594
So everybody say, oh, you
can do one or two nights

00:29:22.594 --> 00:29:24.763
without sleeping and say, how can I sleep?

00:29:24.763 --> 00:29:26.598
I wait that moment since two years.

00:29:26.598 --> 00:29:27.849
I'm so excited.

00:29:27.849 --> 00:29:28.933
I'm so happy to be there.

00:29:28.933 --> 00:29:31.269
And then it's like you you have wings

00:29:31.269 --> 00:29:33.480
so you can fly around the mountain,

00:29:33.480 --> 00:29:34.689
and I'm so happy.

00:29:34.689 --> 00:29:37.442
And then if the race goes like you want,

00:29:37.442 --> 00:29:38.276
then you're okay.

00:29:38.276 --> 00:29:40.820
It would be sunsets and sunrise.

00:29:40.820 --> 00:29:41.946
There will be this pass.

00:29:41.946 --> 00:29:43.698
It's so unbelievable.

00:29:43.698 --> 00:29:46.075
And then, ah, you can fell your sensation,

00:29:46.075 --> 00:29:47.494
you can fell your training,

00:29:47.494 --> 00:29:49.871
you can fell what you
built since 10 years,

00:29:49.871 --> 00:29:51.664
your strategy about food,

00:29:51.664 --> 00:29:52.540
about that land,

00:29:52.540 --> 00:29:53.458
about equipment,

00:29:53.458 --> 00:29:54.501
about material, about family,

00:29:54.501 --> 00:29:56.127
about everything.

00:29:56.127 --> 00:29:57.962
There's a lot of thing.

00:29:57.962 --> 00:29:59.672
And when everything match,

00:30:00.507 --> 00:30:02.008
wow, then you feel it.

00:30:02.008 --> 00:30:05.678
Okay, today, I'm perfect day,

00:30:05.678 --> 00:30:07.263
and you don't feel it.

00:30:07.263 --> 00:30:09.599
And even, I think last year in Hardrock,

00:30:09.599 --> 00:30:12.101
I was even more fast at the
end than at the beginning

00:30:12.101 --> 00:30:14.145
just because I was, wow.

00:30:14.145 --> 00:30:15.855
Today it's just so incredible.

00:30:15.855 --> 00:30:18.733
And I remember with Dakota Jones we play,

00:30:18.733 --> 00:30:21.069
he pace me on the last part,

00:30:21.069 --> 00:30:26.074
and we just playing and we
run all over all the time.

00:30:26.324 --> 00:30:28.451
I say, okay, I'm even faster
than at the beginning.

00:30:28.451 --> 00:30:29.744
It's just crazy,

00:30:29.744 --> 00:30:34.707
and just no matter if
it's 10, 20, 25 hours,

00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:37.001
you just happy,

00:30:37.001 --> 00:30:40.421
and then you can feel that you,

00:30:40.421 --> 00:30:41.756
yeah, you are just flying

00:30:41.756 --> 00:30:44.634
and it's just a very good moment.

00:30:44.634 --> 00:30:49.639
And yeah, this is what I try to,

00:30:50.348 --> 00:30:51.933
these kind of sense of feelings,

00:30:51.933 --> 00:30:55.061
I try to have on a race.

00:30:55.061 --> 00:30:55.895
- Right.

00:30:55.895 --> 00:30:57.856
Your emotional relationship
to the whole thing.

00:30:57.856 --> 00:30:59.858
But as somebody who,

00:30:59.858 --> 00:31:02.235
you have a background
in physiotherapy, right?

00:31:02.235 --> 00:31:05.363
So from like a biological perspective

00:31:05.363 --> 00:31:07.031
or a training perspective,

00:31:07.031 --> 00:31:10.243
are you doing things in training

00:31:10.243 --> 00:31:11.619
that you think others aren't,

00:31:11.619 --> 00:31:14.289
or is there something about your,

00:31:14.289 --> 00:31:15.707
the way that you're built?

00:31:15.707 --> 00:31:18.001
Like, Killian has a crazy VO2 max,

00:31:18.001 --> 00:31:18.835
or you know,

00:31:18.835 --> 00:31:22.130
is there something that
makes you extra well suited

00:31:22.130 --> 00:31:23.673
to this type of sport?

00:31:23.673 --> 00:31:26.134
Or do you think it's just because

00:31:26.134 --> 00:31:27.719
you've been doing it for a long time,

00:31:27.719 --> 00:31:28.720
and like, I don't know.

00:31:28.720 --> 00:31:30.013
I'm trying to wrap my head around.

00:31:30.013 --> 00:31:31.931
- Yeah.
- I'm sure there are

00:31:31.931 --> 00:31:33.933
other people that
participate in these races

00:31:33.933 --> 00:31:35.935
who are very grateful to be there, right?

00:31:35.935 --> 00:31:37.478
And have a love for the mountains.

00:31:37.478 --> 00:31:40.148
So there is something
different going on with you,

00:31:40.148 --> 00:31:41.107
is there not?

00:31:41.107 --> 00:31:43.735
- No, it's right.
(man laughing)

00:31:43.735 --> 00:31:45.612
- I'm trying to make you blush.

00:31:45.612 --> 00:31:47.071
- If I have a scientific approach,

00:31:47.071 --> 00:31:48.364
it's true that,

00:31:48.364 --> 00:31:51.117
yes, I cannot complain
about my performance

00:31:51.117 --> 00:31:52.619
and about my body,

00:31:52.619 --> 00:31:55.705
but I think I have a very
different approach than Killian,

00:31:55.705 --> 00:31:57.332
and I think Killian needs to be different

00:31:57.332 --> 00:31:58.750
because he tried to be,

00:31:58.750 --> 00:32:01.336
to perform on short
distance and long distance.

00:32:01.336 --> 00:32:04.923
So, and I think it's not a secret

00:32:04.923 --> 00:32:08.593
that Killian have some incredible capacity

00:32:08.593 --> 00:32:11.346
and ability in terms of heart
and breath and everything.

00:32:11.346 --> 00:32:13.348
- At a very high level of exertion.

00:32:13.348 --> 00:32:14.432
- And me,

00:32:14.432 --> 00:32:16.267
I practice as a team,

00:32:16.267 --> 00:32:18.645
3000 steeple chase when I was young,

00:32:18.645 --> 00:32:19.479
or cross country,

00:32:19.479 --> 00:32:21.064
and I was not bad,

00:32:21.064 --> 00:32:23.775
but I was not at the top level.

00:32:23.775 --> 00:32:26.110
And I think, okay, I can run fast,

00:32:26.110 --> 00:32:27.028
but not as,

00:32:27.946 --> 00:32:31.824
yes, I was not very, very, very good,

00:32:31.824 --> 00:32:34.035
not the top French performer,

00:32:34.035 --> 00:32:38.498
but I think it was enough for
ultra trail, the distance.

00:32:38.498 --> 00:32:40.291
And so I'm not,

00:32:41.209 --> 00:32:43.544
I don't train just for
ultra trail distance

00:32:43.544 --> 00:32:45.838
because during winter
I made some intensity

00:32:45.838 --> 00:32:46.673
and something like that.

00:32:46.673 --> 00:32:47.507
Not as Killian,

00:32:47.507 --> 00:32:52.512
but more than 90% of people
which practice only ultra trail

00:32:53.721 --> 00:32:56.265
in France, or even in
Europe, or US, I think.

00:32:56.265 --> 00:32:57.433
So I think,

00:32:58.559 --> 00:33:01.521
during winter I work a
lot on my physiology,

00:33:01.521 --> 00:33:04.273
and on intensity, and something like that.

00:33:04.273 --> 00:33:09.237
So I think it's to compare to Killian

00:33:09.696 --> 00:33:10.947
because it's something different.

00:33:10.947 --> 00:33:13.658
But if I compare some to the other

00:33:13.658 --> 00:33:16.244
long distance, ultra distance runner,

00:33:16.244 --> 00:33:20.999
I think on short distance,
I could be better than them,

00:33:20.999 --> 00:33:23.876
but what I like is the
same approach as them.

00:33:23.876 --> 00:33:28.006
It's spend some long day
in the mountains even more,

00:33:28.006 --> 00:33:30.466
so I think I can have the
same endurance trainings

00:33:30.466 --> 00:33:31.509
than them.

00:33:31.509 --> 00:33:32.844
But if I want to push,

00:33:32.844 --> 00:33:35.763
I can push a bit higher than them.

00:33:35.763 --> 00:33:37.598
- Right.
- So it was interesting,

00:33:37.598 --> 00:33:38.766
like last year in UTMB,

00:33:38.766 --> 00:33:40.685
I think we have the same background

00:33:40.685 --> 00:33:43.688
with the five or six as runner,

00:33:43.688 --> 00:33:46.065
but because we play too
much with Jim Walmsley,

00:33:46.065 --> 00:33:49.485
I was just so destroyed after 80K.

00:33:49.485 --> 00:33:52.530
And in the distance, it
was hard for me to go fast,

00:33:52.530 --> 00:33:55.616
but I know that if I want
to push in each ascent,

00:33:55.616 --> 00:34:00.621
I can make like four or five
minutes faster than the other.

00:34:01.539 --> 00:34:03.875
So it was so comfortable for me,

00:34:03.875 --> 00:34:05.668
not comfortable, because painful,

00:34:05.668 --> 00:34:07.378
but it was very interesting for me to say,

00:34:07.378 --> 00:34:10.840
okay, even if I lose three
minutes in each descent,

00:34:10.840 --> 00:34:12.550
it's not so bad

00:34:12.550 --> 00:34:16.345
because I can easily put
them five or four minutes

00:34:16.345 --> 00:34:17.180
in each ascent.

00:34:17.180 --> 00:34:18.431
So I think for me,

00:34:18.431 --> 00:34:21.100
it's very interesting
to have this background

00:34:21.100 --> 00:34:23.019
just to know that okay,

00:34:23.019 --> 00:34:25.938
in ultra distance, I maybe like the other,

00:34:25.938 --> 00:34:28.483
but if I want to push,
I can push a bit more.

00:34:28.483 --> 00:34:30.109
- You have that extra gear.

00:34:30.109 --> 00:34:30.943
- [Francois] Yeah.

00:34:30.943 --> 00:34:33.488
- In your back pocket you
have the confidence to know

00:34:33.488 --> 00:34:35.239
it's fine I'm running with you right now,

00:34:35.239 --> 00:34:37.241
because when we get to
that grade up there,

00:34:37.241 --> 00:34:39.077
I'm gonna put you in the dust.

00:34:39.077 --> 00:34:39.911
(man chuckling)
- I can go.

00:34:39.911 --> 00:34:40.953
(man laughing)

00:34:40.953 --> 00:34:43.331
- So let's talk about the
training a little bit.

00:34:44.248 --> 00:34:47.043
You know, what is the structure to it?

00:34:47.043 --> 00:34:51.214
What is the philosophy of
the day in day out approach?

00:34:51.214 --> 00:34:52.131
You know,

00:34:52.131 --> 00:34:54.342
walk us through what that looks like.

00:34:54.342 --> 00:34:55.301
- Yeah, so I've,

00:34:55.301 --> 00:34:59.013
I try to have a long term
approach on my training,

00:34:59.013 --> 00:35:01.349
and on my race, and on my career.

00:35:01.349 --> 00:35:04.477
So I don't have like a day to day running.

00:35:04.477 --> 00:35:06.437
I don't like to have any routine,

00:35:06.437 --> 00:35:10.608
and I can't because I built
my life totally different

00:35:10.608 --> 00:35:13.653
than normal runner or professional runner,

00:35:13.653 --> 00:35:17.740
because you know what it
means to have some kids.

00:35:17.740 --> 00:35:18.908
(man chuckling)

00:35:18.908 --> 00:35:19.742
But with three kids,

00:35:19.742 --> 00:35:22.995
I have like now nine,
seven, and three years old.

00:35:24.789 --> 00:35:26.707
- It's amazing you have
time to do anything.

00:35:26.707 --> 00:35:27.542
- I want to be there.

00:35:27.542 --> 00:35:29.877
I want to be there with
them and with my wife.

00:35:29.877 --> 00:35:32.588
We want to have some common
project about the wine,

00:35:32.588 --> 00:35:33.756
about creating an event,

00:35:33.756 --> 00:35:34.590
about different things.

00:35:34.590 --> 00:35:37.426
So it's what I want.

00:35:37.426 --> 00:35:38.636
It's not just, okay,

00:35:39.971 --> 00:35:42.056
you can just be a professional.

00:35:42.056 --> 00:35:44.809
Yes, if I want, I can be
a professional runner.

00:35:44.809 --> 00:35:46.435
And if I don't want any kids,

00:35:46.435 --> 00:35:47.770
we can make these choice,

00:35:47.770 --> 00:35:48.980
but we don't want that.

00:35:48.980 --> 00:35:50.565
We want to have a normal life,

00:35:50.565 --> 00:35:51.399
a social life.

00:35:51.399 --> 00:35:53.901
We want to have kids, a family story.

00:35:53.901 --> 00:35:55.903
We want to have a real job

00:35:55.903 --> 00:35:57.280
and to spend some time with that.

00:35:57.280 --> 00:35:59.740
Then okay, I know that.

00:35:59.740 --> 00:36:02.535
So I have to train when I have time.

00:36:02.535 --> 00:36:04.745
And I know that, yes,

00:36:04.745 --> 00:36:07.498
before Hardrock I will have
to spend some long days

00:36:07.498 --> 00:36:08.332
in mountains,

00:36:08.332 --> 00:36:12.044
so that's why I'm here like
two weeks before the race.

00:36:12.044 --> 00:36:14.046
That's why I will live in Raylan Island

00:36:14.046 --> 00:36:16.215
like two weeks now before the race

00:36:16.215 --> 00:36:18.176
because I have to race to beat myself.

00:36:18.176 --> 00:36:20.595
I have to focus more on my training.

00:36:20.595 --> 00:36:22.305
But, but yes,

00:36:22.305 --> 00:36:24.348
I just know that,

00:36:24.348 --> 00:36:27.268
okay, two months before a long race

00:36:27.268 --> 00:36:30.730
you have to spend more
long days in the mountain.

00:36:30.730 --> 00:36:34.483
You have to train
specifically for each race.

00:36:34.483 --> 00:36:35.443
Like for Hardrock,

00:36:35.443 --> 00:36:39.155
I know that one of the
most important thing

00:36:39.155 --> 00:36:41.449
is altitude training.

00:36:41.449 --> 00:36:44.911
So I don't run that much

00:36:44.911 --> 00:36:47.455
like during, since the last two months,

00:36:47.455 --> 00:36:50.833
but I spent a lot of
time in high mountain,

00:36:50.833 --> 00:36:52.835
it wasn't Skimo, it wasn't climbing,

00:36:52.835 --> 00:36:54.212
it was something like that.

00:36:55.213 --> 00:36:56.255
And I think if I compare to last year,

00:36:56.255 --> 00:36:58.216
I run even less,

00:36:58.216 --> 00:37:00.927
but I spend more time in high altitude.

00:37:00.927 --> 00:37:05.932
So, I think it's maybe a
good thing for Hardrock.

00:37:06.057 --> 00:37:09.685
And if I have to go to Raylan
Island at the end of the year,

00:37:09.685 --> 00:37:12.104
I know that it's totally different,

00:37:12.104 --> 00:37:16.234
and I would have to focus
more on distance training,

00:37:16.234 --> 00:37:18.486
something like that to,

00:37:18.486 --> 00:37:20.196
there's a lot of stairs in that island,

00:37:20.196 --> 00:37:23.449
so I have to walk with big
steps or something like that.

00:37:23.449 --> 00:37:26.827
And I try to think like
six months or five months

00:37:26.827 --> 00:37:27.912
before the race,

00:37:27.912 --> 00:37:30.957
okay, what will be specific on that race?

00:37:30.957 --> 00:37:33.167
And then every day, every night,

00:37:33.167 --> 00:37:34.835
every training you think about that,

00:37:34.835 --> 00:37:37.046
okay, what I'm actually doing,

00:37:37.046 --> 00:37:38.881
it's important for next race,

00:37:38.881 --> 00:37:40.299
or it's no matter,

00:37:40.299 --> 00:37:41.926
so I try to don't that.

00:37:41.926 --> 00:37:42.760
- Right, right.

00:37:42.760 --> 00:37:44.679
- And yes, and then I have,

00:37:44.679 --> 00:37:47.723
yes, I try to respect lot the season

00:37:47.723 --> 00:37:51.227
and the condition in the mountain,

00:37:51.227 --> 00:37:54.730
so that's why I choose
that kind of season.

00:37:54.730 --> 00:37:57.984
Actually that's starting my
running season with autumn

00:37:57.984 --> 00:37:59.652
it's just perfect for me

00:37:59.652 --> 00:38:04.490
because there's a lot of
snow from December to May

00:38:04.490 --> 00:38:05.783
where I live.

00:38:05.783 --> 00:38:09.620
So it's hard to be ready
for race in April or May

00:38:09.620 --> 00:38:12.039
because it mean that
you have to take the car

00:38:12.039 --> 00:38:13.833
to go in the valley to train.

00:38:13.833 --> 00:38:16.836
And this is what not what I love.

00:38:16.836 --> 00:38:18.963
It's what I love is running for my door,

00:38:18.963 --> 00:38:20.756
or skiing from my door.
- [Rich] Yeah.

00:38:20.756 --> 00:38:25.052
- So it's easier for me
to practice some Skimo

00:38:25.052 --> 00:38:26.554
from January to May.

00:38:26.554 --> 00:38:28.514
And I think it's a
very, very good training

00:38:28.514 --> 00:38:30.433
for endurance training and for,

00:38:30.433 --> 00:38:32.351
it has strategy for summer,

00:38:32.351 --> 00:38:35.980
then you have to back on running
slowly and progressively.

00:38:35.980 --> 00:38:40.985
And I have all the months
of April, May, and June

00:38:40.985 --> 00:38:42.737
to back on running progressively,

00:38:42.737 --> 00:38:46.032
so it's just perfect
for race, like mid July.

00:38:46.032 --> 00:38:48.242
So that's why I choose
that kind of strategy

00:38:48.242 --> 00:38:50.619
since three to four years now.

00:38:50.619 --> 00:38:52.079
- [Rich] Right.
- Just because I know,

00:38:52.079 --> 00:38:55.374
okay, if I have to train
in March in running,

00:38:55.374 --> 00:38:56.459
(man huffing)

00:38:56.459 --> 00:39:00.212
it would be hard for to get
the motivation in Monterey,

00:39:00.212 --> 00:39:03.007
so that's why I try to
adapt my strategy like that

00:39:03.007 --> 00:39:03.841
and to think;

00:39:03.841 --> 00:39:07.094
like long time ago with
my wife, with my friends,

00:39:07.094 --> 00:39:07.928
with my partner,

00:39:07.928 --> 00:39:09.305
with my current doctor was,

00:39:09.305 --> 00:39:11.682
okay, I will do it next year.

00:39:11.682 --> 00:39:13.225
So I have to focus mid-July,

00:39:13.225 --> 00:39:14.602
I have to focus mid-October,

00:39:14.602 --> 00:39:16.687
so I have to plan everything around that.

00:39:16.687 --> 00:39:19.899
So even about the product development,

00:39:19.899 --> 00:39:22.985
the family events, the
socials, the holidays,

00:39:22.985 --> 00:39:24.070
everything,

00:39:24.070 --> 00:39:26.530
I try to planning in November and December

00:39:26.530 --> 00:39:31.118
and then it's way easier
to train and try everything

00:39:31.118 --> 00:39:33.287
because with my family,

00:39:33.287 --> 00:39:37.958
we know with the kids and
family since last year,

00:39:37.958 --> 00:39:39.710
since one month, one year ago,

00:39:39.710 --> 00:39:41.045
that you can plan-
- Yeah,

00:39:41.045 --> 00:39:42.296
you can plan way ahead.

00:39:42.296 --> 00:39:43.839
Yeah, exactly.
- End of June.

00:39:43.839 --> 00:39:46.759
It's not like if I say
to them one week ago,

00:39:46.759 --> 00:39:48.552
it will be so hard for them.

00:39:48.552 --> 00:39:50.638
But now, since one year we prepare that,

00:39:50.638 --> 00:39:51.889
since one year we know that,

00:39:51.889 --> 00:39:54.809
okay, it will be hard for them and for me

00:39:54.809 --> 00:39:57.978
to be without each other
during three weeks.

00:39:57.978 --> 00:40:00.314
So we have to plan some strategies.

00:40:00.314 --> 00:40:02.775
We visit some friends,

00:40:02.775 --> 00:40:03.818
some family,

00:40:03.818 --> 00:40:05.152
we have some stage,

00:40:05.152 --> 00:40:08.447
we have some different thing
and we prepare us many things,

00:40:08.447 --> 00:40:11.534
so it's easier and we
wait that moment finally

00:40:11.534 --> 00:40:14.537
and we will be so happy to
meet each other in three weeks.

00:40:14.537 --> 00:40:15.996
So it just,

00:40:15.996 --> 00:40:19.417
if if you plan it since
one year or even more,

00:40:19.417 --> 00:40:21.460
it's so easy.

00:40:21.460 --> 00:40:24.004
But if you don't stay true to your people,

00:40:24.004 --> 00:40:25.464
or you, okay.
(man chuckling)

00:40:25.464 --> 00:40:27.174
- See ya later.
- In one month,

00:40:27.174 --> 00:40:31.470
I have my biggest race
of my life and bye bye.

00:40:31.470 --> 00:40:32.471
(man groaning)

00:40:32.471 --> 00:40:34.557
It's so hard.
(man chuckling)

00:40:34.557 --> 00:40:35.683
So this is my,

00:40:35.683 --> 00:40:38.769
it's not like I don't
know if I answer very well

00:40:38.769 --> 00:40:39.603
to your question,

00:40:39.603 --> 00:40:42.106
it's not my strategic of training,

00:40:42.106 --> 00:40:45.484
but planning things like that,

00:40:45.484 --> 00:40:48.028
I think it's a key point of the training

00:40:48.028 --> 00:40:49.280
because then you just have to say,

00:40:49.280 --> 00:40:53.534
okay, we keep some free time for that.

00:40:53.534 --> 00:40:56.245
We plan this event, or
this event, and this event,

00:40:56.245 --> 00:40:59.248
and finally your training
is nearly done like that.

00:40:59.248 --> 00:41:03.002
Because now I'm here two
weeks now before Hardrock.

00:41:03.002 --> 00:41:05.588
I finish all my product development.

00:41:05.588 --> 00:41:08.299
I'm just without family.

00:41:08.299 --> 00:41:09.925
I just have time for me.

00:41:09.925 --> 00:41:10.926
- [Rich] Right.
- What will you do

00:41:10.926 --> 00:41:12.052
when you are in the mountain

00:41:12.052 --> 00:41:13.512
just with free time for you?

00:41:13.512 --> 00:41:14.472
It's training.
- Right.

00:41:14.472 --> 00:41:16.223
- [Francois] It's easy to train.

00:41:16.223 --> 00:41:20.686
- There is something counterintuitive,

00:41:20.686 --> 00:41:25.649
but kind of undeniable
about having a full life

00:41:25.774 --> 00:41:28.027
outside of your life as an athlete.

00:41:28.027 --> 00:41:30.196
You know, you would think

00:41:30.196 --> 00:41:33.407
you would enhance your
performance by living like a monk

00:41:33.407 --> 00:41:34.492
in a cabin alone,

00:41:34.492 --> 00:41:35.993
and just waking up in the morning

00:41:35.993 --> 00:41:37.453
and going out and training all day

00:41:37.453 --> 00:41:39.997
with no distractions year round.

00:41:39.997 --> 00:41:43.125
And perhaps you could
get a great performance

00:41:43.125 --> 00:41:44.668
in the short term,

00:41:44.668 --> 00:41:47.171
but you know, the more I speak to you,

00:41:47.171 --> 00:41:51.258
the more I realize how deeply
you think about longevity.

00:41:51.258 --> 00:41:54.637
It's more about trying to
be the best that you can be

00:41:54.637 --> 00:41:56.555
for the longest period of time.

00:41:56.555 --> 00:41:57.848
And in order to do that,

00:41:57.848 --> 00:42:00.976
you have to have diversity in your life.

00:42:00.976 --> 00:42:03.437
You have to be living your life.

00:42:04.730 --> 00:42:07.733
You can't be putting aside
things that you want in your life

00:42:07.733 --> 00:42:09.401
for the sake of performance.

00:42:09.401 --> 00:42:10.486
So to have three kids,

00:42:10.486 --> 00:42:12.780
to have this full life

00:42:12.780 --> 00:42:14.532
where you're engaged in your community,

00:42:14.532 --> 00:42:18.244
and your previous career as a winemaker,

00:42:18.244 --> 00:42:19.286
which I want to talk about,

00:42:19.286 --> 00:42:20.412
like all of those things

00:42:20.412 --> 00:42:24.458
feel like they would detract
from your performances.

00:42:24.458 --> 00:42:26.544
But my sense is that all of those things

00:42:26.544 --> 00:42:29.129
ultimately enhance your performance.

00:42:29.129 --> 00:42:30.464
They fuel your life

00:42:30.464 --> 00:42:33.384
because you're a happy, grounded person

00:42:33.384 --> 00:42:36.679
with interests outside of just running.

00:42:36.679 --> 00:42:37.721
- Yeah, it's true.

00:42:37.721 --> 00:42:40.474
But it's true too that you are more tired

00:42:40.474 --> 00:42:42.935
and it's not easy to train every day.

00:42:42.935 --> 00:42:45.980
And some, I actually it was a,

00:42:45.980 --> 00:42:49.483
I have a very hard moments
of moments of June,

00:42:49.483 --> 00:42:52.570
and I discuss a lot
with Jim and say, okay,

00:42:52.570 --> 00:42:53.571
(man sighing)

00:42:53.571 --> 00:42:55.531
okay, you don't have any kids.

00:42:55.531 --> 00:42:57.783
He's just in France for training.

00:42:57.783 --> 00:42:59.076
You have just to wake up,

00:42:59.076 --> 00:43:00.160
make his coffee.
- Yeah.

00:43:00.160 --> 00:43:00.995
- And then thinking,

00:43:00.995 --> 00:43:02.788
oh, where can I go today to train?

00:43:02.788 --> 00:43:05.833
And you wake up at six in the
morning because baby's crying,

00:43:05.833 --> 00:43:07.334
then you have to take kids to school,

00:43:07.334 --> 00:43:09.044
then you have then a partner,

00:43:09.044 --> 00:43:09.962
and media to do.

00:43:09.962 --> 00:43:12.673
And then if you have
time you can go to train,

00:43:12.673 --> 00:43:13.799
but you have too many things to do.

00:43:13.799 --> 00:43:15.009
Ah, okay, it's too much.

00:43:15.009 --> 00:43:16.677
How can I prepare from like that?

00:43:16.677 --> 00:43:18.429
But on those other things,

00:43:18.429 --> 00:43:19.805
you think about what you say,

00:43:19.805 --> 00:43:21.473
it's okay, this is my life.

00:43:21.473 --> 00:43:23.392
I choose that one,

00:43:23.392 --> 00:43:24.435
and it's helped me a lot.

00:43:24.435 --> 00:43:29.440
So it's never easy to have this background

00:43:29.648 --> 00:43:30.691
and to have a,

00:43:30.691 --> 00:43:33.402
but I think for me everybody's different.

00:43:33.402 --> 00:43:35.821
But for me it was very
important since the beginning.

00:43:35.821 --> 00:43:38.616
And we discuss a lot of that with my wife

00:43:38.616 --> 00:43:39.908
to have a balanced life,

00:43:39.908 --> 00:43:41.577
to have this different pillar,

00:43:41.577 --> 00:43:42.911
to like, okay, a family,

00:43:42.911 --> 00:43:43.746
social,

00:43:43.746 --> 00:43:46.123
the job, the sport, everything,

00:43:46.123 --> 00:43:47.916
and sport is important,

00:43:47.916 --> 00:43:48.751
but for me,

00:43:48.751 --> 00:43:52.963
I try to never put it a most
important thing in my life.

00:43:53.797 --> 00:43:55.924
I always try to have some background.

00:43:55.924 --> 00:43:57.009
Okay, it's just a pleasure,

00:43:57.009 --> 00:43:58.177
it's just a passion,

00:43:58.177 --> 00:44:01.055
and I think having kids
and something for me

00:44:02.514 --> 00:44:05.601
was always more important than everything,

00:44:05.601 --> 00:44:08.020
because if you focus too much on sport,

00:44:08.020 --> 00:44:11.023
okay, one year, it's everything works.

00:44:11.023 --> 00:44:11.857
Okay, it's perfect.

00:44:11.857 --> 00:44:13.359
But if it's doing 10 years,

00:44:13.359 --> 00:44:17.696
then 10 years you look beside you,

00:44:17.696 --> 00:44:18.530
you look around you and say,

00:44:18.530 --> 00:44:20.407
okay, since 10 year I focus on that.

00:44:20.407 --> 00:44:22.368
And finally I don't have any kids

00:44:22.368 --> 00:44:24.620
and I don't really everything for me.

00:44:24.620 --> 00:44:25.537
I think it's-

00:44:25.537 --> 00:44:26.914
- When your whole sense of identity

00:44:26.914 --> 00:44:30.793
is wrapped up in your performances.

00:44:30.793 --> 00:44:32.336
- Yeah, I think, yeah.

00:44:32.336 --> 00:44:33.170
- Yeah, yeah.

00:44:35.464 --> 00:44:36.965
With respect to the training,

00:44:36.965 --> 00:44:40.427
I've heard you say
something along the lines of

00:44:40.427 --> 00:44:41.679
it's more important,

00:44:41.679 --> 00:44:46.350
the frequency of your
trainings is more important

00:44:46.350 --> 00:44:48.644
than the length of your trainings.

00:44:48.644 --> 00:44:49.478
Like there's this idea,

00:44:49.478 --> 00:44:51.021
if you're gonna be an ultra runner,

00:44:51.021 --> 00:44:53.357
you gotta go out and
run for 12 hours a day

00:44:53.357 --> 00:44:54.733
every single day, right?

00:44:54.733 --> 00:44:57.820
And I think you've said your longer runs

00:44:57.820 --> 00:45:01.573
are really kind of in the
six to seven hour range.

00:45:01.573 --> 00:45:04.451
You'll go out for those longer days of,

00:45:04.451 --> 00:45:05.411
as you mentioned earlier,

00:45:05.411 --> 00:45:07.329
just being in the mountains, Skimo,

00:45:07.329 --> 00:45:08.163
or just, you know,

00:45:08.163 --> 00:45:11.917
kind of hiking or whatever
it is to experience altitude.

00:45:11.917 --> 00:45:14.169
But in terms of the running,

00:45:14.169 --> 00:45:17.798
my sense is that you're
careful not to overdo it

00:45:17.798 --> 00:45:20.259
and go into that kind
of over training zone

00:45:20.259 --> 00:45:22.344
where you can get injured or burnt out.

00:45:22.344 --> 00:45:25.973
- I try to always have
some pain somewhere.

00:45:25.973 --> 00:45:28.392
And I actually have some difficulty

00:45:28.392 --> 00:45:31.019
with some part of my body,

00:45:31.019 --> 00:45:33.939
but I try to make some cycling,

00:45:33.939 --> 00:45:34.898
and to make different things,

00:45:34.898 --> 00:45:37.609
and I try to never push too much

00:45:37.609 --> 00:45:41.029
to be over training or injured.

00:45:41.029 --> 00:45:42.948
So yes, I try to do that.

00:45:42.948 --> 00:45:45.492
But yes,

00:45:45.492 --> 00:45:48.704
it's kind of part of my training too

00:45:48.704 --> 00:45:50.664
to say, okay, I wake up,

00:45:50.664 --> 00:45:51.582
my second kid,

00:45:51.582 --> 00:45:53.709
he wake up like eight times each night

00:45:53.709 --> 00:45:55.002
until he are three years.

00:45:55.002 --> 00:45:56.211
- Wow.

00:45:56.211 --> 00:45:57.296
(man laughing)
- So you can say,

00:45:57.296 --> 00:45:59.590
okay, I'm too tried and I cannot train.

00:45:59.590 --> 00:46:02.134
Or you can say, okay, I will train.

00:46:02.134 --> 00:46:03.093
- You're training when you're tired

00:46:03.093 --> 00:46:04.386
is kind of a good thing.

00:46:04.386 --> 00:46:06.597
- But yes, I was thinking that.

00:46:06.597 --> 00:46:09.308
I was thinking, okay, I'm so tired,

00:46:09.308 --> 00:46:10.642
but I have to train.

00:46:10.642 --> 00:46:13.061
But when you are on a
new trail after 20 hour,

00:46:13.061 --> 00:46:13.896
what do you think?

00:46:13.896 --> 00:46:14.730
You are tired too.

00:46:14.730 --> 00:46:16.774
So if you never train when you are tired,

00:46:16.774 --> 00:46:18.567
you will never have this feeling.

00:46:18.567 --> 00:46:22.613
So me say, okay, I will
train with less intensity

00:46:22.613 --> 00:46:23.447
of course,

00:46:23.447 --> 00:46:26.533
maybe we less energy of course,

00:46:26.533 --> 00:46:30.454
but I will train anyway even if I'm tired,

00:46:30.454 --> 00:46:32.414
even if I drink too much the day before,

00:46:32.414 --> 00:46:35.042
if I made too much party even.

00:46:35.042 --> 00:46:37.544
Okay, it's even if I eat too much,

00:46:37.544 --> 00:46:39.338
even if just I have my breakfast.

00:46:39.338 --> 00:46:40.297
Okay.

00:46:40.297 --> 00:46:41.632
You have to test everything

00:46:41.632 --> 00:46:45.302
because in your trail
you will meet everything.

00:46:45.302 --> 00:46:49.348
And in trail, what we said
earlier is that you cannot,

00:46:49.348 --> 00:46:50.766
you can plan everything,

00:46:50.766 --> 00:46:54.561
but you will have to adapt everything.

00:46:54.561 --> 00:46:56.647
- [Rich] Yeah.
- Because this is why

00:46:56.647 --> 00:46:57.481
we made ultra.

00:46:57.481 --> 00:47:00.150
If we know what will happen,

00:47:00.150 --> 00:47:03.737
we can make athletes more
cross country or some loop.

00:47:03.737 --> 00:47:05.906
But no, we go in the mountain,

00:47:05.906 --> 00:47:07.866
in high mountain

00:47:07.866 --> 00:47:11.745
just because we want to
have something different.

00:47:11.745 --> 00:47:13.997
We will have to adapt ourself,

00:47:13.997 --> 00:47:16.583
and that's why I think my life,

00:47:16.583 --> 00:47:18.335
maybe it's good for ultra distance

00:47:18.335 --> 00:47:21.672
because okay, this morning we're in US,

00:47:22.548 --> 00:47:23.382
we want to train,

00:47:23.382 --> 00:47:26.343
your scrambled eggs and
bacon and everything.

00:47:26.343 --> 00:47:27.594
But then okay, we will run.

00:47:27.594 --> 00:47:31.598
Okay, but I won't have to
wait three hours for running

00:47:31.598 --> 00:47:33.809
and I have to train directly,

00:47:33.809 --> 00:47:34.643
so, oh, okay.

00:47:34.643 --> 00:47:37.563
I feel ill, I feel thirsty.

00:47:37.563 --> 00:47:40.899
Okay, I feel a bit
tired about the jet lag.

00:47:40.899 --> 00:47:41.733
Okay.

00:47:41.733 --> 00:47:45.028
But if I have to wait that
everything is correct to run,

00:47:45.028 --> 00:47:47.030
okay, I will run in one week.

00:47:47.030 --> 00:47:48.240
So no, it's not good.

00:47:48.240 --> 00:47:50.534
So, okay, yesterday we arrive,

00:47:50.534 --> 00:47:53.579
we have a 24 day of traveling,

00:47:53.579 --> 00:47:55.330
but okay, I'm in Boulder.

00:47:55.330 --> 00:47:56.623
I'm happy to be there.

00:47:56.623 --> 00:47:59.042
I would like to discover the mountain,

00:47:59.042 --> 00:48:01.795
so I go there for two hour run.

00:48:01.795 --> 00:48:04.798
For sure I don't have the
best feeling of my life,

00:48:04.798 --> 00:48:07.092
even the worst feeling of my life.

00:48:07.092 --> 00:48:08.760
I sweat a lot.

00:48:08.760 --> 00:48:11.513
I don't have any poor, but-

00:48:11.513 --> 00:48:13.140
- This is the thing though.

00:48:13.140 --> 00:48:13.974
- I think this is the thing,

00:48:13.974 --> 00:48:17.436
and this is really a good
training I think for ultra,

00:48:17.436 --> 00:48:18.812
because you have to adapt,

00:48:18.812 --> 00:48:20.856
you have to feel what's
happening in your body,

00:48:20.856 --> 00:48:22.566
how you can answer,

00:48:22.566 --> 00:48:24.568
and readapt and make things,

00:48:24.568 --> 00:48:27.654
and finally I was able to run two hours.

00:48:27.654 --> 00:48:29.156
And I think it's a good thing.

00:48:29.156 --> 00:48:32.409
But if your whole life is well planned

00:48:32.409 --> 00:48:37.414
to always be at the best
possibility for your training,

00:48:37.789 --> 00:48:39.499
when you arrive in ultra, you don't.

00:48:39.499 --> 00:48:41.001
- You're gonna be waiting for a long time.

00:48:41.001 --> 00:48:42.502
- You don't know how to do, yeah.

00:48:42.502 --> 00:48:43.337
- Right.

00:48:43.337 --> 00:48:44.671
Right, you're missing the whole point.

00:48:44.671 --> 00:48:45.756
- [Francois] Yeah.
- All right.

00:48:45.756 --> 00:48:49.635
- Of course, when you arrive
in Colorado after 10 hour,

00:48:49.635 --> 00:48:51.136
middle of the night,

00:48:51.136 --> 00:48:54.514
of course your legs are destroyed.

00:48:54.514 --> 00:48:58.477
Of course you run 10 hour
too fast with descent,

00:48:58.477 --> 00:48:59.311
ascent,

00:48:59.311 --> 00:49:01.063
and then it's middle of the night,

00:49:01.063 --> 00:49:03.065
of course you feel tired

00:49:03.065 --> 00:49:05.484
and you don't know what's happened

00:49:05.484 --> 00:49:06.735
because you don't want to eat.

00:49:06.735 --> 00:49:08.654
Of course, because it's
middle of the night,

00:49:08.654 --> 00:49:10.656
nobody eats at the middle of the night.

00:49:10.656 --> 00:49:12.074
- [Rich] Yeah.
- So you don't feel

00:49:12.074 --> 00:49:12.908
comfortable.

00:49:12.908 --> 00:49:16.828
But if your body was
never in that position,

00:49:16.828 --> 00:49:18.205
you don't know how to do.

00:49:18.205 --> 00:49:22.376
But if your body was, okay,
I remember I did that,

00:49:22.376 --> 00:49:24.044
or I have this same feeling,

00:49:24.044 --> 00:49:26.672
or okay, I can do it because
I have the experience

00:49:26.672 --> 00:49:27.506
that I can,

00:49:27.506 --> 00:49:28.340
then you continue

00:49:28.340 --> 00:49:31.635
and then you can be a
better part of yourself

00:49:31.635 --> 00:49:33.428
and even win the race.

00:49:33.428 --> 00:49:38.433
But that's why I think my
life is not finally so bad

00:49:39.685 --> 00:49:41.228
for ultra training.
- Right.

00:49:41.228 --> 00:49:42.813
- Maybe for altitude, and performance,

00:49:42.813 --> 00:49:44.189
and short distance training,

00:49:44.189 --> 00:49:45.148
but for ultra?

00:49:45.148 --> 00:49:46.566
- Every training session,

00:49:46.566 --> 00:49:48.026
you're combating an obstacle, right?

00:49:48.026 --> 00:49:50.070
- [Francois] Yeah.
- Just to get out the door.

00:49:50.070 --> 00:49:51.488
- Exactly.

00:49:51.488 --> 00:49:54.658
- Yeah, that is a really
interesting lens to look at it.

00:49:55.534 --> 00:49:59.621
How has your training
evolved over the years?

00:49:59.621 --> 00:50:03.125
I mean, with every win or miss,

00:50:03.125 --> 00:50:05.711
you know, all of these accomplishments

00:50:05.711 --> 00:50:07.254
you're learning along the way,

00:50:07.254 --> 00:50:10.716
and I assume refining, figuring
out what works for you,

00:50:10.716 --> 00:50:12.759
what doesn't,

00:50:12.759 --> 00:50:15.637
Did you do anything different this year

00:50:15.637 --> 00:50:17.556
leading up to Hardrock

00:50:17.556 --> 00:50:20.892
versus leading up to Hardrock last year?

00:50:20.892 --> 00:50:21.852
- Yeah, of course.

00:50:21.852 --> 00:50:23.353
I try to,

00:50:23.353 --> 00:50:27.107
normally I never did a race from one year

00:50:27.107 --> 00:50:28.817
to the next year directly

00:50:28.817 --> 00:50:32.487
because you have too many
elements of comparison

00:50:32.487 --> 00:50:33.321
and it's too hard for me.

00:50:33.321 --> 00:50:34.489
- [Rich] Yeah.
- And you put

00:50:34.489 --> 00:50:35.574
too much pressure.

00:50:35.574 --> 00:50:39.244
But it's a bits a game of the Hardrock.

00:50:39.244 --> 00:50:40.829
But when you want it,

00:50:40.829 --> 00:50:43.582
then it's interesting to
come back the year after

00:50:43.582 --> 00:50:45.709
because you run with all the way

00:50:46.710 --> 00:50:47.711
for the community.

00:50:47.711 --> 00:50:49.671
I think it's very nice to come back

00:50:49.671 --> 00:50:51.423
and I'm so happy to be there again.

00:50:51.423 --> 00:50:54.926
So I have to compose with that.

00:50:54.926 --> 00:50:59.931
But yes, last year I feel
that the altitude training,

00:51:00.640 --> 00:51:02.976
it's something very important,

00:51:02.976 --> 00:51:07.606
so that I was really
focused a bit more on that.

00:51:07.606 --> 00:51:10.150
And I tried to build some
project around Mont Blanc,

00:51:10.150 --> 00:51:12.778
which is highest mountain in Europe,

00:51:12.778 --> 00:51:15.280
but the condition were
not so good this year

00:51:15.280 --> 00:51:17.199
because it was really dry.

00:51:17.199 --> 00:51:19.868
So I made some more, some rock climbing.

00:51:19.868 --> 00:51:22.287
We go to in Switzerland and Italy.

00:51:23.246 --> 00:51:24.623
Apennine seven,

00:51:24.623 --> 00:51:26.166
I don't know if you knows this mountain,

00:51:26.166 --> 00:51:28.418
but it's a very great mountain.

00:51:28.418 --> 00:51:33.381
And we spent some more than
20 hour above 4,000 meters.

00:51:33.381 --> 00:51:35.342
And I did Mont Blanc Skimo

00:51:35.342 --> 00:51:37.385
and I went a lot like that.

00:51:37.385 --> 00:51:38.762
So I think altitude training,

00:51:38.762 --> 00:51:41.807
and I'm better than last year.

00:51:41.807 --> 00:51:44.392
But just about training,

00:51:44.392 --> 00:51:47.229
I think because it's a life,

00:51:47.229 --> 00:51:50.732
and we try to create an event with my wife

00:51:50.732 --> 00:51:52.567
for next September.

00:51:52.567 --> 00:51:54.319
It's first edition.

00:51:54.319 --> 00:51:58.031
So I was not thinking

00:51:58.031 --> 00:52:02.369
that it will take this
amount of time to us,

00:52:02.369 --> 00:52:07.207
and so I don't have the time
that I was thinking to have

00:52:07.207 --> 00:52:09.251
for training, just for running.

00:52:09.251 --> 00:52:13.296
So I think I'm a bit less
trained than last year

00:52:13.296 --> 00:52:14.131
in training,

00:52:14.131 --> 00:52:16.508
and even more in decent

00:52:16.508 --> 00:52:17.467
because of the,

00:52:19.010 --> 00:52:22.931
we enjoy to spend many
times around this event,

00:52:22.931 --> 00:52:24.099
and to discuss about that,

00:52:24.099 --> 00:52:26.393
and we really want to make something.

00:52:27.561 --> 00:52:29.062
Yes, something good

00:52:29.062 --> 00:52:31.148
and something very linked with our values.

00:52:31.148 --> 00:52:32.858
So it was very important for us.

00:52:32.858 --> 00:52:37.863
It was one of our priority
this past two months.

00:52:38.530 --> 00:52:40.824
So I hope I will, it will be okay.

00:52:40.824 --> 00:52:43.243
And we still have like
10 days for training,

00:52:43.243 --> 00:52:44.828
so I hope it'll be okay,

00:52:44.828 --> 00:52:48.790
but I think that I'm
more trained on altitude,

00:52:48.790 --> 00:52:52.210
but less trained just
in the running capacity.

00:52:52.210 --> 00:52:53.336
- Right, got it.

00:52:53.336 --> 00:52:55.964
So yes, you have this new race

00:52:55.964 --> 00:52:59.134
that you and your wife have
created called Ultra Spirit?

00:52:59.134 --> 00:53:00.343
- Yes.
- Ultra Spirit,

00:53:00.343 --> 00:53:01.928
which is coming up in September,

00:53:01.928 --> 00:53:03.180
early September, right?

00:53:03.180 --> 00:53:04.514
- [Francois] Yes.

00:53:04.514 --> 00:53:05.432
- Which is exciting.

00:53:05.432 --> 00:53:07.184
You're creating your own race.

00:53:07.184 --> 00:53:11.563
It's a couple races between
25 and 50 kilometers

00:53:11.563 --> 00:53:13.940
in your region where you live.

00:53:13.940 --> 00:53:17.235
And this is a new kind of
entrepreneurial journey.

00:53:18.069 --> 00:53:19.738
Prior to that you were a winemaker,

00:53:19.738 --> 00:53:20.864
which I want to get into,

00:53:20.864 --> 00:53:24.910
but what inspired you
to create your own race?

00:53:24.910 --> 00:53:28.538
- It's a bit like a of consequence

00:53:28.538 --> 00:53:31.374
of why we stop the winery,

00:53:32.500 --> 00:53:35.045
and yes, for us it was
really important to,

00:53:35.045 --> 00:53:35.962
it's not really a race,

00:53:35.962 --> 00:53:38.882
it's more like an event
I think, ultra distance,

00:53:38.882 --> 00:53:41.009
because we were thinking,

00:53:41.009 --> 00:53:44.054
okay, like in five years or 10 years,

00:53:44.054 --> 00:53:47.557
if we want to do
something in the mountain,

00:53:47.557 --> 00:53:51.144
something organized in the
mountain, what it will be?

00:53:51.144 --> 00:53:52.229
And we were thinking,

00:53:52.229 --> 00:53:55.357
I'm not sure we'll go again in UTMB,

00:53:55.357 --> 00:53:56.274
maybe yes.

00:53:56.274 --> 00:53:59.945
Or I'm not sure we'll go
again a classical for trail.

00:53:59.945 --> 00:54:03.615
I think we would like to be together

00:54:03.615 --> 00:54:06.076
to share something like as a team.

00:54:06.076 --> 00:54:08.662
We would like to have some good moment

00:54:08.662 --> 00:54:10.247
with the other participant.

00:54:10.247 --> 00:54:12.123
Even with the organizer.

00:54:12.123 --> 00:54:15.835
We would like to be in total
immersion with the territory

00:54:15.835 --> 00:54:18.672
and the specialty,

00:54:18.672 --> 00:54:23.677
and we won't like to
discover like very deeply

00:54:23.927 --> 00:54:25.303
the place where we are,

00:54:25.303 --> 00:54:28.515
and to have some fun,

00:54:28.515 --> 00:54:32.686
learn the basics, which is ultra trail.

00:54:32.686 --> 00:54:35.522
So we say, okay, we
actually organize something,

00:54:35.522 --> 00:54:39.609
like who can answer out of that.

00:54:39.609 --> 00:54:40.819
And we were thinking just,

00:54:40.819 --> 00:54:45.824
okay, what could be very nice for us

00:54:45.907 --> 00:54:47.158
in five years to have,

00:54:47.158 --> 00:54:49.202
and then we organize that event.

00:54:49.202 --> 00:54:52.414
- Yeah, and so it's a
team based thing, right?

00:54:52.414 --> 00:54:53.832
- [Francois] Yes.
- 25 teams,

00:54:53.832 --> 00:54:55.417
three people on a team.

00:54:55.417 --> 00:54:56.668
- Yeah.
- [Rich] Is it like a relay,

00:54:56.668 --> 00:54:58.211
or you run together with your teammates?

00:54:58.211 --> 00:54:59.045
- No, no, no.

00:54:59.045 --> 00:55:00.880
You start together, and
you finish together,

00:55:00.880 --> 00:55:02.048
and you sleep together,

00:55:02.048 --> 00:55:03.300
and you eat together,

00:55:03.300 --> 00:55:05.135
and you sleep in a tent of three people

00:55:05.135 --> 00:55:07.595
without any shower during two days.

00:55:07.595 --> 00:55:09.931
So it'll be a-
- It's like a reality show.

00:55:09.931 --> 00:55:12.976
- It will be a very nice
experience for three people.

00:55:12.976 --> 00:55:17.063
But with the team, between the team too,

00:55:17.063 --> 00:55:20.650
I think because this year
we start just with 25 team,

00:55:20.650 --> 00:55:25.071
and I think that will be
some very good relationship

00:55:25.071 --> 00:55:26.448
in the,

00:55:26.448 --> 00:55:27.907
and will be interesting.

00:55:27.907 --> 00:55:30.618
And one thing interesting too is that,

00:55:30.618 --> 00:55:32.495
okay, performance is important,

00:55:32.495 --> 00:55:36.791
and the time of running
will be important too,

00:55:36.791 --> 00:55:38.835
but I think what is the most important

00:55:38.835 --> 00:55:40.420
is to to be in the mountain,

00:55:40.420 --> 00:55:41.588
to discover yourself,

00:55:41.588 --> 00:55:42.714
to discover your team,

00:55:42.714 --> 00:55:43.840
to discover each other.

00:55:43.840 --> 00:55:47.969
So that's why everybody will
run the same amount of time.

00:55:47.969 --> 00:55:51.598
So you will start the Friday for six hour,

00:55:51.598 --> 00:55:53.725
then you will have 11 hour on Saturday,

00:55:53.725 --> 00:55:56.144
and then you are five
hour again on the Sunday.

00:55:56.144 --> 00:55:58.855
So it will be around
20, 21 hour of running

00:55:58.855 --> 00:55:59.856
during the weekend,

00:55:59.856 --> 00:56:01.649
which it's not nothing.

00:56:01.649 --> 00:56:05.278
But it's not like 21 hour in one time.

00:56:05.278 --> 00:56:08.114
And everybody will run
the same amount of time,

00:56:08.114 --> 00:56:10.784
which is very difficult
for us as organizer,

00:56:10.784 --> 00:56:13.870
because you have to
think that the first team

00:56:13.870 --> 00:56:16.039
will run faster than the last team.

00:56:16.039 --> 00:56:18.041
- [Rich] Yeah.
- So they will make some

00:56:19.167 --> 00:56:23.380
different loop to arrive
all together at the end.

00:56:23.380 --> 00:56:26.925
We would like that people
arrive in less than 30 minutes.

00:56:26.925 --> 00:56:30.887
So it would be very
interesting to organize it,

00:56:30.887 --> 00:56:34.391
and yeah, I hope it would
be fun for the people

00:56:34.391 --> 00:56:37.769
and we will make some different
activity at the middle.

00:56:37.769 --> 00:56:39.521
Like, you arrive at
the top on the mountain

00:56:39.521 --> 00:56:42.816
and you arrive to make a game

00:56:42.816 --> 00:56:46.694
just to understand what is the difference

00:56:46.694 --> 00:56:48.822
between the summer trees
and the winter trees,

00:56:48.822 --> 00:56:52.534
which is impossible at
the middle of a race.

00:56:52.534 --> 00:56:54.786
But then if you are not able to do that,

00:56:54.786 --> 00:56:57.163
you will have a penalty of 25 minutes.

00:56:57.163 --> 00:56:57.997
- Ah!

00:56:57.997 --> 00:57:00.375
The twist.
- Yes.

00:57:00.375 --> 00:57:03.294
People will say, okay, no
matter if I run fast or not,

00:57:03.294 --> 00:57:05.630
I most have to focus on my test.

00:57:05.630 --> 00:57:07.424
(man laughing)
And so it would be interesting

00:57:07.424 --> 00:57:09.926
because you will have
like 10 games like that

00:57:09.926 --> 00:57:11.886
during the three days.
- That's cool.

00:57:11.886 --> 00:57:13.721
- And during the day, during the night.

00:57:13.721 --> 00:57:16.766
And I think it's really
different than a normal race.

00:57:16.766 --> 00:57:19.185
- So you could be the fastest runners,

00:57:19.185 --> 00:57:21.312
but if you fail all those, you won't,

00:57:21.312 --> 00:57:22.272
other tests.
- Yeah,

00:57:22.272 --> 00:57:23.648
you wont won the competition.

00:57:23.648 --> 00:57:27.193
- Right.
(man laughing)

00:57:27.193 --> 00:57:28.486
That's a great spin on the whole thing.

00:57:28.486 --> 00:57:29.654
- And we try to make something

00:57:29.654 --> 00:57:32.991
that even if you are the
faster and the stronger runner,

00:57:32.991 --> 00:57:34.993
it's not sure that you will win the game.

00:57:34.993 --> 00:57:38.204
The game not only on the spot think.

00:57:38.204 --> 00:57:39.164
- Right.

00:57:39.164 --> 00:57:41.166
Yeah, I like that approach.

00:57:41.166 --> 00:57:45.670
I, just the other day I did a
podcast with Malcolm Gladwell,

00:57:45.670 --> 00:57:46.504
who's a writer.

00:57:46.504 --> 00:57:47.380
I don't know if you're familiar with him,

00:57:47.380 --> 00:57:49.299
but he's also, he's super into running,

00:57:49.299 --> 00:57:53.303
and he always is thinking
about ways to change the way

00:57:53.303 --> 00:57:55.555
that we do sports to make
them more interesting.

00:57:55.555 --> 00:57:59.601
And he had this idea that high
school cross country teams

00:58:01.311 --> 00:58:03.730
it should be reconfigured such that

00:58:03.730 --> 00:58:08.485
it's not about whoever wins
the race for that team,

00:58:08.485 --> 00:58:10.487
but it's the combined time of like,

00:58:10.487 --> 00:58:12.489
you know, the 10 people on the team.

00:58:12.489 --> 00:58:15.492
So the slowest person on the
team is just as important

00:58:15.492 --> 00:58:16.451
as the fastest.

00:58:16.451 --> 00:58:20.288
And so everybody, you're
incentivized as a team

00:58:20.288 --> 00:58:23.958
to cheer for the least talented person

00:58:23.958 --> 00:58:25.710
or the least well trained
person on your team,

00:58:25.710 --> 00:58:28.296
which is similar to the
idea that you just shared.

00:58:28.296 --> 00:58:31.007
Like, how can you even the playing field

00:58:31.007 --> 00:58:33.635
and make it kind of up
for grabs for anybody?

00:58:33.635 --> 00:58:35.345
It's not just about the best athlete.

00:58:35.345 --> 00:58:38.723
- Yeah, and it's even we vote TVT.

00:58:38.723 --> 00:58:41.226
If you run in a team of three,

00:58:41.226 --> 00:58:43.853
I think the best team will not be

00:58:43.853 --> 00:58:46.731
the team of the best free runner.

00:58:46.731 --> 00:58:48.149
It will be the team

00:58:48.149 --> 00:58:51.069
who will take care the
most of the third runner.

00:58:51.069 --> 00:58:52.654
- [Rich] Right.
- Because the third runner,

00:58:52.654 --> 00:58:55.114
the slowest runner, is
the most important one.

00:58:55.114 --> 00:58:57.450
And if you don't take care of each other,

00:58:57.450 --> 00:58:58.409
you will be not able to finish.

00:58:58.409 --> 00:58:59.994
- Doesn't matter.
(man laughing)

00:58:59.994 --> 00:59:03.331
- And that's why, even at
the registration I say,

00:59:03.331 --> 00:59:07.961
okay, you have to stop at
least 25 minutes for everybody.

00:59:09.212 --> 00:59:12.549
With that, the registration
will be more cool moments,

00:59:12.549 --> 00:59:13.675
family can come,

00:59:13.675 --> 00:59:15.218
and you have time to discover,

00:59:15.218 --> 00:59:16.928
and to discuss with each other,

00:59:16.928 --> 00:59:19.681
and you will have time to
take care of the third runner.

00:59:19.681 --> 00:59:21.140
If doing 25 minutes,

00:59:21.140 --> 00:59:24.936
you don't take care of the
those person of your group.

00:59:24.936 --> 00:59:26.479
I think it's a mistake,

00:59:26.479 --> 00:59:29.065
because if you arrive
the first runner is easy.

00:59:29.065 --> 00:59:30.942
He can, yes, change your shoes.

00:59:30.942 --> 00:59:31.818
Edge out the runner,

00:59:31.818 --> 00:59:33.111
even made a message,

00:59:33.111 --> 00:59:37.782
or okay, ask and change
the nutrition strategy,

00:59:37.782 --> 00:59:38.616
and help him,

00:59:38.616 --> 00:59:39.701
and it will,

00:59:39.701 --> 00:59:41.744
it can change a lot

00:59:41.744 --> 00:59:45.081
because I think it's very
important to know that

00:59:45.081 --> 00:59:48.042
because then if they want to make a ultra,

00:59:48.042 --> 00:59:51.045
they will have more
experience and more idea

00:59:51.045 --> 00:59:52.755
about what can happen in ultra.

00:59:52.755 --> 00:59:54.882
And I think all the activity,

00:59:54.882 --> 00:59:58.011
it looks like, okay, tasting your cheese.

00:59:58.011 --> 01:00:00.430
This is no, no, no, no.

01:00:00.430 --> 01:00:01.681
- Nothing to do with it.

01:00:01.681 --> 01:00:03.057
- Nothing to do with it, yeah.

01:00:03.057 --> 01:00:04.100
But finally,

01:00:04.100 --> 01:00:08.229
if you think each activity
will have a sense for yourself,

01:00:08.229 --> 01:00:09.105
for your team,

01:00:09.105 --> 01:00:10.315
and for your experience,

01:00:10.315 --> 01:00:11.983
and your way in ultra.

01:00:11.983 --> 01:00:16.988
And that's what we would
like to to show to people

01:00:16.988 --> 01:00:17.822
at the end,

01:00:17.822 --> 01:00:20.033
is that, okay, you did 10 activities,

01:00:20.033 --> 01:00:21.451
you did three days,

01:00:21.451 --> 01:00:23.286
you don't need an ultra,

01:00:23.286 --> 01:00:24.996
but we, all of that,

01:00:24.996 --> 01:00:28.666
I think for your next ultra
you will be more ready.

01:00:28.666 --> 01:00:29.500
- Right.

01:00:29.500 --> 01:00:30.793
And it makes it more fun.

01:00:30.793 --> 01:00:34.714
So that person who's trying
something for the first time

01:00:34.714 --> 01:00:36.341
will have a positive experience

01:00:36.341 --> 01:00:40.094
that will make them enthusiastic
about learning more.

01:00:40.094 --> 01:00:41.346
- We hope so.

01:00:41.346 --> 01:00:42.597
We will have fun,

01:00:42.597 --> 01:00:44.515
and we hope that they will have fun too,

01:00:44.515 --> 01:00:46.434
otherwise we missed something.

01:00:46.434 --> 01:00:47.393
(man laughing)

01:00:47.393 --> 01:00:48.311
- So this is,

01:00:48.311 --> 01:00:51.314
you know, a lot of people
perhaps expected you

01:00:51.314 --> 01:00:56.110
to show up at UTMB again
and go for a fifth win.

01:00:56.110 --> 01:00:57.403
These dates coincide.

01:00:57.403 --> 01:00:59.030
That makes that impossible.

01:00:59.030 --> 01:00:59.864
Is it,

01:00:59.864 --> 01:01:02.575
was that I assume this is why

01:01:02.575 --> 01:01:04.327
you're not participating in UTMB,

01:01:04.327 --> 01:01:05.787
or is it just like I did that.

01:01:05.787 --> 01:01:07.413
I don't need to go back there.

01:01:07.413 --> 01:01:09.624
What is your relationship to that race?

01:01:09.624 --> 01:01:12.043
- I'm not sure I will
go back into the future

01:01:12.043 --> 01:01:14.712
because I did already five times,

01:01:14.712 --> 01:01:16.631
and I win it four times,

01:01:16.631 --> 01:01:18.633
and I did three times CCCs.

01:01:18.633 --> 01:01:22.345
I'm not sure I will go back to UTMB.

01:01:22.345 --> 01:01:23.638
I cannot promise it 100%,

01:01:23.638 --> 01:01:27.350
but maybe I will go back
and a bit different,

01:01:27.350 --> 01:01:28.393
and with some other people.

01:01:28.393 --> 01:01:29.227
I don't know.

01:01:29.227 --> 01:01:31.437
But for sure it's not my goal

01:01:31.437 --> 01:01:33.940
to to be the first to win it five times,

01:01:33.940 --> 01:01:35.358
or six time, or even four times.

01:01:35.358 --> 01:01:36.943
Because last year everybody say,

01:01:37.819 --> 01:01:39.821
oh, you are here to be the
first to win it four times.

01:01:41.280 --> 01:01:42.240
Okay, if you want.

01:01:42.240 --> 01:01:43.116
But not really.

01:01:43.116 --> 01:01:44.784
- That wasn't your motivation.

01:01:44.784 --> 01:01:45.618
- No, no, no.

01:01:45.618 --> 01:01:46.452
It's not my motivation.

01:01:46.452 --> 01:01:49.122
And I think that's why I win it four time.

01:01:49.122 --> 01:01:51.124
It's just because it
was not my motivation.

01:01:51.124 --> 01:01:56.129
But no, for me, trail running
means some different things.

01:01:56.421 --> 01:02:00.383
Some travel, some
discovering some other race.

01:02:00.383 --> 01:02:03.594
And I think there's many,
many, many races in the world,

01:02:03.594 --> 01:02:05.972
and yeah, I think it's,

01:02:05.972 --> 01:02:07.807
UTMB's, it's important.

01:02:07.807 --> 01:02:10.393
It's a very nice race, an incredible race.

01:02:10.393 --> 01:02:12.812
And even if people say,
ah, it's too crowded.

01:02:12.812 --> 01:02:14.355
Now there's too much people.

01:02:14.355 --> 01:02:17.108
And it's a big race, a big mess.

01:02:17.108 --> 01:02:19.610
Okay, Chamonix is Chamonix.

01:02:19.610 --> 01:02:21.404
UTMB's UTMB,

01:02:21.404 --> 01:02:24.157
and even River Race,

01:02:24.157 --> 01:02:25.241
when we go to race when you are here,

01:02:25.241 --> 01:02:28.035
and you say, okay, you have to cross

01:02:28.035 --> 01:02:29.245
three different country,

01:02:29.245 --> 01:02:32.457
you have to make a loop
around this amazing mountain.

01:02:33.541 --> 01:02:34.667
It's amazing.

01:02:34.667 --> 01:02:38.713
It's very wonderful and
I really enjoy that,

01:02:38.713 --> 01:02:41.466
that part of France and of the Alp.

01:02:41.466 --> 01:02:44.427
And yeah, for me it's, when I think UTMB,

01:02:44.427 --> 01:02:46.929
it's very good memories.

01:02:46.929 --> 01:02:49.515
And for sure I will be
there again one time,

01:02:49.515 --> 01:02:52.185
but I'm not sure I will
race again to win it,

01:02:52.185 --> 01:02:54.812
because I did it,

01:02:54.812 --> 01:02:56.856
and I have many, many other goals,

01:02:56.856 --> 01:03:00.610
and I want to to discover something else,

01:03:00.610 --> 01:03:03.070
and to travel and to
make something different.

01:03:03.070 --> 01:03:05.156
- [Rich] Yeah.
- And I have many, many plans

01:03:05.156 --> 01:03:07.992
in my head for the next few runs.

01:03:07.992 --> 01:03:08.826
- Yeah.

01:03:08.826 --> 01:03:09.786
Well, I think it's cool

01:03:09.786 --> 01:03:12.371
that you're always kind
of iterating and growing,

01:03:12.371 --> 01:03:15.333
and not afraid to kind
of let go of things,

01:03:15.333 --> 01:03:16.626
to try new things.

01:03:16.626 --> 01:03:19.545
Which kind of brings up
the wine making thing.

01:03:19.545 --> 01:03:24.217
I mean, for years your wife and
yourself were creating wine,

01:03:24.217 --> 01:03:25.051
right?

01:03:25.051 --> 01:03:26.052
In Beaujolais region.

01:03:26.052 --> 01:03:27.762
You've since moved to the mountains.

01:03:27.762 --> 01:03:30.014
But talk a little bit about that.

01:03:30.014 --> 01:03:32.683
Like, that's a world I
know very little about,

01:03:32.683 --> 01:03:37.688
but feels like it would be an
all consuming kind of affair

01:03:37.980 --> 01:03:40.775
to create great wine.

01:03:40.775 --> 01:03:41.692
- Yeah, it was.

01:03:41.692 --> 01:03:43.194
It was very,

01:03:43.194 --> 01:03:47.198
and for UTMB, it just a smaller
joke I would like to add.

01:03:47.198 --> 01:03:48.825
It's just that I start,

01:03:48.825 --> 01:03:50.618
I don't want to go back to UTMB

01:03:50.618 --> 01:03:53.162
because I really would like
that an American winner

01:03:53.162 --> 01:03:55.122
could win it for the first time.

01:03:55.122 --> 01:03:56.958
- Oh.
(men laughing)

01:03:56.958 --> 01:03:59.085
That's very sweet of you.

01:03:59.085 --> 01:04:00.294
That's the pull quote.

01:04:00.294 --> 01:04:01.170
We'll take that out.

01:04:01.170 --> 01:04:03.881
That's that's the thing
you're gonna get quoted on.

01:04:03.881 --> 01:04:05.132
(man chuckling)
- I just-

01:04:05.132 --> 01:04:07.844
- Any American in particular
you might be thinking of?

01:04:09.095 --> 01:04:11.264
- It's no, I called the American runner,

01:04:11.264 --> 01:04:14.809
but yes, I have one of
them not far from my house,

01:04:14.809 --> 01:04:16.811
and I hope he could be.

01:04:16.811 --> 01:04:19.438
- I think he's doing everything
in his power right now

01:04:19.438 --> 01:04:21.607
to make that happen just for you.

01:04:21.607 --> 01:04:22.441
- Sure.

01:04:22.441 --> 01:04:24.402
And now, but the wine was,

01:04:25.236 --> 01:04:27.363
yeah, the one was really passionate,

01:04:27.363 --> 01:04:28.197
but to be honest,

01:04:28.197 --> 01:04:32.785
at the beginning we were
not thinking that this job

01:04:32.785 --> 01:04:36.289
is so passionate, and so complete,

01:04:36.289 --> 01:04:38.332
and so different every day.

01:04:38.332 --> 01:04:41.377
We were just thinking that okay,

01:04:41.377 --> 01:04:44.171
we like each other with my wife.

01:04:44.171 --> 01:04:47.466
We get married since
11 years, two days ago.

01:04:47.466 --> 01:04:48.301
- [Rich] Ah, great.

01:04:48.301 --> 01:04:50.261
(man chuckling)
- So, yeah,

01:04:50.261 --> 01:04:51.429
we are really close,

01:04:51.429 --> 01:04:54.640
and we want to build something together,

01:04:54.640 --> 01:04:57.059
but we were thinking, okay, I'm physio.

01:04:57.059 --> 01:04:58.895
I'm an international runner.

01:04:58.895 --> 01:05:01.272
She works from an array.

01:05:01.272 --> 01:05:03.399
I work on my way.

01:05:03.399 --> 01:05:06.402
There's too many things and
we never see each other,

01:05:06.402 --> 01:05:09.655
and it's not the way that
we want to spend our life,

01:05:09.655 --> 01:05:11.741
so we have to have a common project.

01:05:11.741 --> 01:05:14.827
And what we like is to be out,

01:05:14.827 --> 01:05:16.078
to be the natural,

01:05:16.078 --> 01:05:19.916
to feel the terre.

01:05:19.916 --> 01:05:20.917
I don't know if it's a good word.

01:05:20.917 --> 01:05:22.710
- The land.
- [Francois] Yeah, the land.

01:05:22.710 --> 01:05:24.670
- The soil.
- And the roots.

01:05:24.670 --> 01:05:26.923
And it's very important for us.

01:05:26.923 --> 01:05:30.217
And so we were thinking maybe
we will have some animals,

01:05:30.217 --> 01:05:34.305
maybe we would have a
bed and breakfast house,

01:05:34.305 --> 01:05:36.807
and share something
with the people locally

01:05:36.807 --> 01:05:37.975
and something like that.

01:05:37.975 --> 01:05:41.520
And maybe we can have this possibility

01:05:41.520 --> 01:05:44.315
to make this winery.

01:05:44.315 --> 01:05:46.317
It's an old story.

01:05:46.317 --> 01:05:48.110
We were family,

01:05:48.110 --> 01:05:49.779
but not as close as we think,

01:05:49.779 --> 01:05:53.115
but it's helped a lot for us.

01:05:53.115 --> 01:05:54.992
But we were thinking, okay, animals,

01:05:54.992 --> 01:05:56.202
you have to be there every day.

01:05:56.202 --> 01:05:57.411
And bed and breakfast,

01:05:57.411 --> 01:05:58.496
exactly the same.

01:05:58.496 --> 01:06:01.040
And we have international runner careers

01:06:01.040 --> 01:06:01.874
that may be possible.

01:06:01.874 --> 01:06:04.961
So maybe the winery
could be the best option.

01:06:04.961 --> 01:06:08.714
And that's why we say, okay,
we will try this option.

01:06:08.714 --> 01:06:11.050
And then we discover this.

01:06:11.050 --> 01:06:13.219
We knew that we like the wine,

01:06:13.219 --> 01:06:15.221
we like to taste some different wine

01:06:15.221 --> 01:06:17.098
even when we are in US or in France.

01:06:17.098 --> 01:06:19.642
It's just so interesting to see that.

01:06:19.642 --> 01:06:22.395
Okay, in Zataria it's totally different.

01:06:22.395 --> 01:06:24.563
Zataria, there's a history

01:06:24.563 --> 01:06:26.107
from this version to this version.

01:06:26.107 --> 01:06:28.693
And we are really
fascinated about the taste,

01:06:28.693 --> 01:06:31.237
and about the finning, and
the history, and everything.

01:06:31.237 --> 01:06:33.781
So we knew that it would be something that

01:06:33.781 --> 01:06:34.865
very passion for us.

01:06:34.865 --> 01:06:39.412
But then we had discovered
that each season

01:06:39.412 --> 01:06:41.205
is totally different,

01:06:41.205 --> 01:06:44.500
and each moment of the
season is totally different

01:06:44.500 --> 01:06:47.253
because you have to
focus on commercializing,

01:06:47.253 --> 01:06:48.421
of communication,

01:06:48.421 --> 01:06:49.755
of creating the bottles,

01:06:49.755 --> 01:06:50.881
on the vinification,

01:06:50.881 --> 01:06:52.008
on the worker,

01:06:52.008 --> 01:06:53.009
on the vineyard.

01:06:53.009 --> 01:06:56.053
And each moment it's totally different.

01:06:56.053 --> 01:06:59.348
And it was so helpful for
us to discover everything

01:06:59.348 --> 01:07:00.307
and to play with that.

01:07:00.307 --> 01:07:03.728
So it was a, a full, full, full-time job.

01:07:03.728 --> 01:07:05.229
But it was so interesting,

01:07:05.229 --> 01:07:08.566
and we have an amazing
10 years on the vineyard,

01:07:08.566 --> 01:07:11.110
and yes, we really enjoy that,

01:07:11.110 --> 01:07:13.696
and we developed some many,
many project about that

01:07:14.613 --> 01:07:16.615
during the pandemic.

01:07:16.615 --> 01:07:19.910
We developed something
like bit more ecological.

01:07:19.910 --> 01:07:23.122
It's to bring the wine from
the valley to the mountain

01:07:24.415 --> 01:07:26.167
by foot instead of helicopter.

01:07:26.167 --> 01:07:27.001
- Oh wow.

01:07:27.001 --> 01:07:27.835
- [Francois] It was very interesting.

01:07:27.835 --> 01:07:28.753
Very hard.
- Yeah.

01:07:28.753 --> 01:07:30.337
But very interesting.

01:07:30.337 --> 01:07:33.174
But this project, even if we stop,

01:07:33.174 --> 01:07:34.717
we want to continue it.

01:07:34.717 --> 01:07:37.386
And I was there last Monday,

01:07:37.386 --> 01:07:38.804
like two days ago,

01:07:38.804 --> 01:07:41.307
to bring two different during the day,

01:07:41.307 --> 01:07:43.934
and it was like eight hour working

01:07:43.934 --> 01:07:46.812
with 30 kilo on your backpack.

01:07:46.812 --> 01:07:51.150
And it's so interesting to
bring the wine from the valley

01:07:51.150 --> 01:07:51.984
to the earth,

01:07:51.984 --> 01:07:56.197
even if some other things
that came to by agriculture,

01:07:56.197 --> 01:07:59.742
at least the wine came back by foot.

01:07:59.742 --> 01:08:04.121
- The idea is that for
sustainability reasons,

01:08:04.121 --> 01:08:05.623
or just to say this is possible?

01:08:05.623 --> 01:08:07.124
- It's not just for sustainability,

01:08:07.124 --> 01:08:08.501
but it's just to show the people

01:08:08.501 --> 01:08:11.170
you bring directly from the producer,

01:08:11.170 --> 01:08:12.588
to the consumer,

01:08:12.588 --> 01:08:16.425
and even it's true that
there's a sustainability part.

01:08:16.425 --> 01:08:18.010
It's really important for us,

01:08:18.010 --> 01:08:21.138
but it's just people, they
will take a glass of wine,

01:08:21.138 --> 01:08:23.390
they know from where the wine is coming.

01:08:23.390 --> 01:08:26.060
They know how the wine
is coming to the earth

01:08:26.060 --> 01:08:27.978
and then you are with your
friends in the mountain

01:08:27.978 --> 01:08:30.064
with the sunset.

01:08:30.064 --> 01:08:31.232
Take your glass of wine.

01:08:31.232 --> 01:08:33.526
I think it's a totally different wine.

01:08:33.526 --> 01:08:34.860
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:08:34.860 --> 01:08:35.945
I can see that.

01:08:35.945 --> 01:08:38.531
And I know you were growing,

01:08:38.531 --> 01:08:41.242
you're doing it organic, or
at least one of the wines

01:08:41.242 --> 01:08:42.076
was organic.
- Yeah,

01:08:42.076 --> 01:08:45.412
it was one of the things
that why we have to stop

01:08:45.412 --> 01:08:48.249
is because it's a lot of cost.

01:08:48.249 --> 01:08:49.750
- It's a lot harder to do that.

01:08:49.750 --> 01:08:51.335
- We are not the owner of the land,

01:08:51.335 --> 01:08:54.755
and it's maybe too much money to continue

01:08:54.755 --> 01:08:56.048
in our way for them,

01:08:56.048 --> 01:08:57.466
and then with the kids.

01:08:57.466 --> 01:08:58.968
And it was too,

01:08:58.968 --> 01:09:01.679
it means too much traveling
for me from the mountain place

01:09:01.679 --> 01:09:03.764
where we are actually to the Beaujolais.

01:09:03.764 --> 01:09:05.349
So it's many, many things that we say,

01:09:05.349 --> 01:09:07.810
okay, we did it for 11 years,

01:09:07.810 --> 01:09:11.021
maybe it's time to switch
from something else,

01:09:11.021 --> 01:09:13.649
and we really want to focus on that event.

01:09:13.649 --> 01:09:16.694
So it's many, many reasons that we change,

01:09:16.694 --> 01:09:18.904
but this kind of project we resort,

01:09:18.904 --> 01:09:20.030
we want to continue it

01:09:20.030 --> 01:09:22.783
because it is very, very interesting.

01:09:22.783 --> 01:09:25.369
And yeah, tonight,

01:09:26.954 --> 01:09:29.248
I don't know if you will taste it tonight,

01:09:29.248 --> 01:09:30.749
but I have some wine for you.

01:09:30.749 --> 01:09:32.084
Maybe you will taste it with your family.

01:09:32.084 --> 01:09:33.878
- We'll see.
- [Francois] To enjoy it.

01:09:33.878 --> 01:09:34.837
(man chuckling)

01:09:34.837 --> 01:09:36.130
- It's,

01:09:36.130 --> 01:09:37.965
well that's a different conversation,

01:09:39.091 --> 01:09:40.634
about my relationship with wine.

01:09:40.634 --> 01:09:41.552
But anyway,

01:09:43.721 --> 01:09:45.431
Beaujolais is,

01:09:45.431 --> 01:09:48.559
I mean it's not that
far from Geneva, right?

01:09:48.559 --> 01:09:50.853
It's fairly close, but you're
not in the mountains, right?

01:09:50.853 --> 01:09:52.605
- So you in US, it's not far.

01:09:52.605 --> 01:09:53.647
(men laughing)
- Yeah,

01:09:53.647 --> 01:09:54.732
it looks close on the map to me.

01:09:54.732 --> 01:09:56.775
For you, you think it's like.

01:09:56.775 --> 01:09:58.694
It's a couple hours in the car, right?

01:09:58.694 --> 01:10:00.905
- Yeah, two hours, yes.
- [Rich] That's nothing.

01:10:00.905 --> 01:10:02.865
- No, it's not that big, but.

01:10:02.865 --> 01:10:05.034
- But for you to train day in a day after.

01:10:05.034 --> 01:10:07.119
- The mountain is totally different, yes.

01:10:07.119 --> 01:10:08.037
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:10:08.037 --> 01:10:12.291
So instead of having to go
back and forth with the kids,

01:10:12.291 --> 01:10:14.084
it's like, let's simplify our lives.

01:10:14.084 --> 01:10:15.252
You moved to the mountains.

01:10:15.252 --> 01:10:19.548
- Yeah, because it means
that we were living

01:10:20.925 --> 01:10:21.926
in the Beaujolais place

01:10:21.926 --> 01:10:23.761
and in the Beaujolais place

01:10:23.761 --> 01:10:25.012
at a different moment of the year,

01:10:25.012 --> 01:10:27.932
so they have to change the
school two times a year.

01:10:27.932 --> 01:10:29.141
And for them it's,

01:10:29.141 --> 01:10:31.060
I can understand that it's a bit hard,

01:10:31.060 --> 01:10:32.561
and yes, many, many reason.

01:10:32.561 --> 01:10:34.688
And now we live yes, in a small village

01:10:34.688 --> 01:10:37.107
in the heart of the Alps.

01:10:37.107 --> 01:10:41.403
And for training it's
really, really better for me.

01:10:41.403 --> 01:10:45.574
And I think for life it's more sustainable

01:10:45.574 --> 01:10:48.285
and it's more interesting for us.

01:10:48.285 --> 01:10:49.328
And yeah, it was,

01:10:49.328 --> 01:10:51.956
it was hard for when you
change something in your life.

01:10:51.956 --> 01:10:54.625
It's always hard to make the move.

01:10:54.625 --> 01:10:58.462
But I think we are happy
with our new choice

01:10:58.462 --> 01:11:02.508
and I hope we will enjoy
it for a long time.

01:11:02.508 --> 01:11:03.342
Yeah.

01:11:03.342 --> 01:11:04.176
- And from a parenting perspective,

01:11:04.176 --> 01:11:06.220
I mean, and your kids are still so young,

01:11:06.220 --> 01:11:10.266
but to kind of raise them in
that mountain environment,

01:11:10.266 --> 01:11:12.101
you know, I would assume on some level

01:11:12.101 --> 01:11:14.561
you're exposing them to this,

01:11:14.561 --> 01:11:17.815
the kind of activities that you love.

01:11:17.815 --> 01:11:19.608
They'll grow up with that.

01:11:19.608 --> 01:11:21.944
They'll have their own minds
about what they want to do

01:11:21.944 --> 01:11:22.778
of course,

01:11:22.778 --> 01:11:25.781
but you have a sense of whether
one or more of your kids

01:11:25.781 --> 01:11:28.158
is prone to the kind of things

01:11:28.158 --> 01:11:30.244
that you like to do?

01:11:30.244 --> 01:11:32.162
Or is it too early to tell?

01:11:32.162 --> 01:11:35.499
- Yeah, we don't want to
push themself too much

01:11:35.499 --> 01:11:38.794
on what we did and on
the competition approach,

01:11:38.794 --> 01:11:42.298
because already people do it for us.

01:11:42.298 --> 01:11:43.632
Are you like your father?

01:11:43.632 --> 01:11:44.967
You will do that?

01:11:44.967 --> 01:11:45.801
- No, no, no.
- No.

01:11:45.801 --> 01:11:47.344
- [Francois] We try to.
- It never works out

01:11:47.344 --> 01:11:48.178
like that.
- But it's true

01:11:48.178 --> 01:11:51.015
that they don't have a TV at home.

01:11:51.015 --> 01:11:55.728
It's true that they're
always, always in the nature.

01:11:55.728 --> 01:11:57.021
- Outdoors.
- In the mountain,

01:11:57.021 --> 01:11:58.564
and there's not too many cars,

01:11:58.564 --> 01:11:59.857
and there's,

01:11:59.857 --> 01:12:03.485
yes, it's a totally different life

01:12:03.485 --> 01:12:05.863
that if you live in a city for sure,

01:12:05.863 --> 01:12:08.198
and it's a very small school.

01:12:08.198 --> 01:12:10.743
There's not too many children

01:12:10.743 --> 01:12:12.619
and they all know each other,

01:12:12.619 --> 01:12:14.621
and yeah,

01:12:14.621 --> 01:12:16.290
during winter times they ski

01:12:16.290 --> 01:12:19.043
like two times or three
times a week with the school

01:12:19.043 --> 01:12:21.754
and two times or three
times a week with the club

01:12:21.754 --> 01:12:23.047
and one time with me,

01:12:23.047 --> 01:12:27.217
so it means that they can
ski like six times a week.

01:12:27.217 --> 01:12:29.053
It's just, yes.
- Yeah.

01:12:29.053 --> 01:12:30.971
- It's sure that they,

01:12:30.971 --> 01:12:34.516
for sure they will be
fascinated about snow,

01:12:34.516 --> 01:12:35.351
about mountain,

01:12:35.351 --> 01:12:36.310
about everything,

01:12:36.310 --> 01:12:41.315
and yeah, when they
came with us to the hut,

01:12:42.399 --> 01:12:43.817
they are so happy to sleep in the hut

01:12:43.817 --> 01:12:47.654
and they already made like
800 meters elevation gain

01:12:47.654 --> 01:12:48.906
at six years old

01:12:48.906 --> 01:12:52.493
because I have three box
of wines on my backpack,

01:12:52.493 --> 01:12:55.329
so they know that I cannot rail them.

01:12:55.329 --> 01:12:56.288
So it's okay,

01:12:56.288 --> 01:12:57.664
I have to go by myself

01:12:57.664 --> 01:13:01.126
because my father have
already four box of wine.

01:13:01.126 --> 01:13:02.461
So they did it finally.

01:13:02.461 --> 01:13:05.464
And sometimes they even
did it faster than us

01:13:05.464 --> 01:13:07.049
because we four box of wine.

01:13:07.049 --> 01:13:07.883
(man laughing)

01:13:07.883 --> 01:13:09.551
Not so easy.

01:13:09.551 --> 01:13:10.386
So, yeah.
- [Rich] That's cool.

01:13:10.386 --> 01:13:13.889
- It's sure that, yeah, they enjoy,

01:13:13.889 --> 01:13:15.516
I hope they enjoy their
life in the mountain,

01:13:15.516 --> 01:13:18.894
but yeah, they have smiles every day,

01:13:18.894 --> 01:13:19.978
so it's okay.
- That's cool.

01:13:19.978 --> 01:13:22.314
And the wine, even though
you're not doing it anymore,

01:13:22.314 --> 01:13:23.482
I mean there's still,

01:13:23.482 --> 01:13:25.025
you have plenty of wine
still to sell, right?

01:13:25.025 --> 01:13:26.985
- Yeah, yeah.
- For years to come.

01:13:26.985 --> 01:13:29.530
So do you have that available

01:13:29.530 --> 01:13:31.532
at some of these races in Europe?

01:13:31.532 --> 01:13:33.784
Like, how do you distribute that?

01:13:33.784 --> 01:13:37.371
- Yeah, we try to just
make direct selling,

01:13:37.371 --> 01:13:38.705
so directly to the people.

01:13:38.705 --> 01:13:41.834
So we choose like three
to four event every year,

01:13:41.834 --> 01:13:42.668
not too much,

01:13:42.668 --> 01:13:46.713
because it's important for
us to take time to discuss

01:13:46.713 --> 01:13:48.090
and to spend some time with people.

01:13:48.090 --> 01:13:50.592
So it's been a lot of energy.

01:13:50.592 --> 01:13:54.680
So we just choose like four
to five event every year

01:13:54.680 --> 01:13:58.058
to sell it and to share
it with the people.

01:13:58.058 --> 01:13:58.892
But yeah,

01:13:58.892 --> 01:14:00.561
I think for the next two to three years

01:14:00.561 --> 01:14:04.356
we have the possibility to still sell it.

01:14:04.356 --> 01:14:09.361
And we made some different
trail runner box every year.

01:14:09.403 --> 01:14:11.196
So we made the last one

01:14:11.196 --> 01:14:14.450
and we will be releasing
that in two months, I think.

01:14:14.450 --> 01:14:18.454
It'll be ready for the end of the season.

01:14:18.454 --> 01:14:21.039
And it's a very interesting one that,

01:14:21.039 --> 01:14:25.586
we try to relate all the
history of the last 10 years.

01:14:25.586 --> 01:14:29.173
It's a mix between running
and creating the wine.

01:14:29.173 --> 01:14:32.593
So we made a lot of jug
and instruction about that.

01:14:32.593 --> 01:14:35.471
So for us, it's a bit emotional

01:14:35.471 --> 01:14:38.223
that this last box.

01:14:38.223 --> 01:14:40.934
- Yeah, so running and drinking wine

01:14:40.934 --> 01:14:43.687
combined into one experience.

01:14:43.687 --> 01:14:45.189
- Yes.
- [Rich] Yeah.

01:14:45.189 --> 01:14:46.607
And normally for people,

01:14:46.607 --> 01:14:47.524
it's not a,

01:14:47.524 --> 01:14:50.402
it's not like a good runner approach

01:14:50.402 --> 01:14:52.446
or a good athlete approach.

01:14:52.446 --> 01:14:55.991
But now we discuss a lot together

01:14:55.991 --> 01:14:59.828
and you can understand that
finally with my way to train

01:14:59.828 --> 01:15:01.413
and my way to life,

01:15:01.413 --> 01:15:04.333
it's not impossible to have a winery

01:15:04.333 --> 01:15:06.627
and to drink a glass of wine

01:15:06.627 --> 01:15:08.879
at the end of your training
and be a top athlete.

01:15:10.464 --> 01:15:12.633
Because I think it's important to say

01:15:12.633 --> 01:15:14.760
that if you spend 10
hours in the mountain,

01:15:14.760 --> 01:15:15.594
then okay,

01:15:15.594 --> 01:15:16.720
you can arrive and drink nothing

01:15:16.720 --> 01:15:20.849
and just eat some veggies
and going to sleep,

01:15:20.849 --> 01:15:23.727
or otherwise, you can
say, okay, I run 10 hour,

01:15:23.727 --> 01:15:25.354
and it was a very good training,

01:15:25.354 --> 01:15:27.606
and I was with some
friends in the mountain,

01:15:27.606 --> 01:15:29.566
and now I have to have a
social moment with them.

01:15:29.566 --> 01:15:32.110
It could be a coffee, or
glass of wine, or beer,

01:15:32.110 --> 01:15:32.945
or whatever you want,

01:15:32.945 --> 01:15:34.780
but for me it's important to say,

01:15:34.780 --> 01:15:36.782
okay, it was amazing day.

01:15:36.782 --> 01:15:39.034
And then when you will be in the race,

01:15:39.034 --> 01:15:41.286
and if you think, okay,

01:15:41.286 --> 01:15:42.663
is that training of 10 hour,

01:15:42.663 --> 01:15:43.664
then I said to my friend,

01:15:43.664 --> 01:15:45.082
no, I cannot come with you

01:15:45.082 --> 01:15:46.959
because I have to make my compacts,

01:15:46.959 --> 01:15:48.460
and I have to sleep early,

01:15:48.460 --> 01:15:49.795
and I have to do nothing,

01:15:49.795 --> 01:15:53.882
and you will remember when
it'll be a hard moment doing so,

01:15:53.882 --> 01:15:54.716
okay.

01:15:54.716 --> 01:15:55.551
It'll be hard training

01:15:55.551 --> 01:15:57.761
and then I don't have a
good moment with my friends.

01:15:57.761 --> 01:15:59.805
I was by myself in my room

01:15:59.805 --> 01:16:01.974
and it was hard again,

01:16:01.974 --> 01:16:03.976
or you can remember, okay,
it was a hard training,

01:16:03.976 --> 01:16:06.019
but it was so good training,

01:16:06.019 --> 01:16:08.605
and then I have a so nice
moment with some friends,

01:16:08.605 --> 01:16:11.525
and we have a nice dinner
and we have a nice moment.

01:16:11.525 --> 01:16:12.734
Wow, it was so good.

01:16:12.734 --> 01:16:14.861
And then you have a positive attitude

01:16:14.861 --> 01:16:15.737
and you can continue,

01:16:15.737 --> 01:16:18.615
and for me, it's my approach to say, okay,

01:16:18.615 --> 01:16:19.408
okay, it's hard,

01:16:19.408 --> 01:16:20.409
but I know it'll be hard,

01:16:20.409 --> 01:16:23.829
but at least I have this very
nice training in my back,

01:16:23.829 --> 01:16:26.623
and it's so good to think
about that at this moment.

01:16:26.623 --> 01:16:29.126
So that's why I try to enjoy that.

01:16:29.126 --> 01:16:31.086
And that's why I say to people, okay,

01:16:31.086 --> 01:16:33.922
I won't say to you drink a bottle of wine

01:16:33.922 --> 01:16:35.674
just one hour before the race,

01:16:35.674 --> 01:16:38.218
but like one week before
or even two months before

01:16:38.218 --> 01:16:41.305
when I saw people, no, I
cannot taste your wine.

01:16:41.305 --> 01:16:43.390
I have UTMB in three months.

01:16:43.390 --> 01:16:45.726
I say, wow, three months before the race,

01:16:45.726 --> 01:16:47.019
you don't want to taste the wine?

01:16:47.019 --> 01:16:48.895
One glass of my wine?

01:16:48.895 --> 01:16:51.857
Okay, maybe you push too much restraint.

01:16:51.857 --> 01:16:53.358
- Yeah, exactly.

01:16:53.358 --> 01:16:56.236
And it goes back to what we
were talking at the beginning

01:16:56.236 --> 01:16:58.697
about longevity in your career.

01:16:58.697 --> 01:17:01.992
You have to enjoy what you're doing,

01:17:01.992 --> 01:17:02.868
if you're gonna stay in it.

01:17:02.868 --> 01:17:06.330
And ultimately the more
you're enjoying this pursuit,

01:17:06.330 --> 01:17:08.498
as hard as it is,

01:17:08.498 --> 01:17:11.501
the the kind of higher
you'll be able to reach,

01:17:11.501 --> 01:17:12.336
you know?

01:17:12.336 --> 01:17:17.299
But to live under such a
strict kind of rule book,

01:17:17.507 --> 01:17:19.217
maybe you have one great year,

01:17:19.217 --> 01:17:22.137
but in five years you're not
gonna wanna do it anymore.

01:17:22.137 --> 01:17:24.222
- I think if it's too hard for you body,

01:17:24.222 --> 01:17:25.057
it's not good.

01:17:25.057 --> 01:17:26.183
But everybody's different.

01:17:26.183 --> 01:17:29.811
Some people they like to
have a life like that,

01:17:29.811 --> 01:17:30.646
like athlete life,

01:17:30.646 --> 01:17:33.815
and they can do it for
a decade no problem.

01:17:33.815 --> 01:17:35.859
And I know some athlete like that,

01:17:35.859 --> 01:17:37.444
and even Killian,

01:17:37.444 --> 01:17:42.449
I think his passion is not
about food, or social moment,

01:17:42.574 --> 01:17:43.408
or something like that,

01:17:43.408 --> 01:17:45.911
but his passion is like that.

01:17:45.911 --> 01:17:48.330
But people will say, I really like wine,

01:17:48.330 --> 01:17:50.165
but I cannot have a glass of wine

01:17:50.165 --> 01:17:52.584
because in six months I will do this race.

01:17:53.669 --> 01:17:56.797
How can this kind of people
continue this for 20 years?

01:17:56.797 --> 01:17:57.881
It's impossible.
- [Rich] Sure.

01:17:57.881 --> 01:17:59.675
- Because, for me, it's not possible.

01:17:59.675 --> 01:18:03.679
So you have to be well
balanced with what you think,

01:18:03.679 --> 01:18:05.681
what you feel, and what you love,

01:18:05.681 --> 01:18:07.974
and then you can think about longevity,

01:18:07.974 --> 01:18:10.811
and I think for short distance
it's a different thing,

01:18:10.811 --> 01:18:12.938
but for a long distance,

01:18:12.938 --> 01:18:16.149
I think it's the best
approach to be well balanced

01:18:16.149 --> 01:18:18.443
and to enjoy what you do every day.

01:18:18.443 --> 01:18:21.154
I think it's very, very important for me.

01:18:21.154 --> 01:18:24.282
- And so how old are you now, 36?

01:18:24.282 --> 01:18:25.200
- Yes.
- 36.

01:18:25.200 --> 01:18:28.537
So how long do you imagine yourself

01:18:28.537 --> 01:18:30.288
being competitive in the sport?

01:18:31.123 --> 01:18:34.000
- I hope for many years,

01:18:34.000 --> 01:18:39.005
but yes, I try to do what I love,

01:18:39.840 --> 01:18:43.135
and I don't want to change my way of life.

01:18:43.135 --> 01:18:46.847
So if in five years, I don't know,

01:18:46.847 --> 01:18:48.306
the level increase a lot,

01:18:48.306 --> 01:18:50.684
and another one on one mys
became more and more athletic,

01:18:50.684 --> 01:18:53.270
and more and more competition,

01:18:53.270 --> 01:18:55.564
and more like you have
to change your life,

01:18:55.564 --> 01:18:59.234
and stop to have a normal life and family

01:18:59.234 --> 01:19:02.237
beside your training to
be able to reach the top.

01:19:03.155 --> 01:19:04.781
It's no matter for me, I will continue.

01:19:04.781 --> 01:19:07.367
I hope I will continue
and I will do it again.

01:19:07.367 --> 01:19:08.827
Maybe not as the first position,

01:19:08.827 --> 01:19:11.580
but I don't want to stop running

01:19:11.580 --> 01:19:13.540
and I don't want to stop traveling

01:19:13.540 --> 01:19:15.167
and discovering some new races

01:19:15.167 --> 01:19:16.835
and meet a community like that.

01:19:16.835 --> 01:19:18.462
- [Rich] Yeah.
- And to have some project,

01:19:18.462 --> 01:19:22.257
but maybe I won't be the
top in five to 10 years,

01:19:22.257 --> 01:19:23.717
but I'm sure I will,

01:19:23.717 --> 01:19:26.094
I'm able to continue to progress.

01:19:26.094 --> 01:19:29.973
Maybe I will progress less
than the top competitors,

01:19:29.973 --> 01:19:33.560
but I'm sure I'm able
to continue to progress

01:19:33.560 --> 01:19:37.481
because I think I
continue to experience my,

01:19:39.399 --> 01:19:40.984
yes, my life.

01:19:40.984 --> 01:19:45.489
And I'm sure I will have
some new things to discover.

01:19:45.489 --> 01:19:46.323
- Right.

01:19:46.323 --> 01:19:48.575
You've created a life that's
conducive to the training,

01:19:48.575 --> 01:19:52.454
but also to the kind of
joyful pursuit of all,

01:19:52.454 --> 01:19:55.916
like everything seems like
it's in a nice balance

01:19:55.916 --> 01:19:58.210
that will allow you to
con continue to do it.

01:19:58.210 --> 01:20:00.921
Whether you're able to
be on a podium or not

01:20:00.921 --> 01:20:03.882
almost feels secondary from
the way that you explained it.

01:20:03.882 --> 01:20:04.716
- Yeah.

01:20:04.716 --> 01:20:08.136
And since, I don't know, maybe 10 years,

01:20:08.136 --> 01:20:10.722
no, but, yeah, I think 10 years now,

01:20:10.722 --> 01:20:12.349
I try to have some project

01:20:14.017 --> 01:20:15.477
inclusive-
- Other things.

01:20:15.477 --> 01:20:16.812
- Of the races.

01:20:16.812 --> 01:20:20.232
And I did, we discussed a lot
about that with Jim Walmsley

01:20:20.232 --> 01:20:21.274
and some of the runner,

01:20:21.274 --> 01:20:24.736
and I'm sure even if it's not on the race

01:20:24.736 --> 01:20:26.446
or on classical race,

01:20:26.446 --> 01:20:30.492
I'm sure I would be able to
continue some different project.

01:20:30.492 --> 01:20:32.035
I never been in Himalaya

01:20:32.035 --> 01:20:34.788
and I think it's some incredible mountain

01:20:34.788 --> 01:20:37.290
and some incredible project to do race in,

01:20:37.290 --> 01:20:39.751
and I'm really passionated when I,

01:20:39.751 --> 01:20:43.755
I heard a story about No
Lands not far from there,

01:20:43.755 --> 01:20:48.134
and it'll be so interesting
to make it like differently,

01:20:48.134 --> 01:20:49.427
with Jim maybe

01:20:49.427 --> 01:20:52.889
to spend some hours in the mountain,

01:20:52.889 --> 01:20:56.810
like for 25 or 30 or 40 hours
in the mountain together.

01:20:56.810 --> 01:20:59.437
And yeah, I discuss with Jim.

01:20:59.437 --> 01:21:01.481
He joined me on the Pacific Crest,

01:21:01.481 --> 01:21:03.650
on the John Muir Trail in 2017.

01:21:03.650 --> 01:21:06.862
Jim was with me on the
Pacific Crest try in 2019.

01:21:09.614 --> 01:21:12.075
And it's so interesting,

01:21:12.075 --> 01:21:14.369
and there's a cool other
trail just over there.

01:21:14.369 --> 01:21:17.455
And I have ton of project
that I would like to do

01:21:17.455 --> 01:21:18.290
in trail running,

01:21:18.290 --> 01:21:21.626
and I think it's the most
important goal for me.

01:21:21.626 --> 01:21:24.004
Is more important than winning that race.

01:21:24.004 --> 01:21:25.630
That race is just, wow,

01:21:25.630 --> 01:21:28.216
what I have to do in the next 10 years.

01:21:28.216 --> 01:21:29.593
Plenty of things, I think.

01:21:29.593 --> 01:21:30.844
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:21:32.262 --> 01:21:34.514
Before we kind of round this out,

01:21:34.514 --> 01:21:39.102
there are plenty of runners
that listen to this show,

01:21:40.270 --> 01:21:41.521
and aspiring runners,

01:21:41.521 --> 01:21:44.774
people who are thinking about
perhaps their first trail race

01:21:44.774 --> 01:21:46.818
or their first ultra marathon,

01:21:46.818 --> 01:21:48.820
so I thought it would be
great if you could share

01:21:48.820 --> 01:21:50.447
maybe some wisdom around

01:21:53.241 --> 01:21:56.494
what are some common
mistakes that people make

01:21:56.494 --> 01:21:59.289
that you see in training
for their first race,

01:21:59.289 --> 01:22:04.294
or in being kind of maybe too afraid

01:22:04.794 --> 01:22:07.923
to sign up for something
that seems impossible to do?

01:22:07.923 --> 01:22:09.466
Like, how do you think about that?

01:22:09.466 --> 01:22:12.969
Or you know, what would
you say to that person?

01:22:12.969 --> 01:22:14.512
- Yeah, I think the progression

01:22:14.512 --> 01:22:16.473
is something very, very important.

01:22:16.473 --> 01:22:20.769
I know that maybe it's
because of the media,

01:22:20.769 --> 01:22:23.229
the people to say the grand,

01:22:23.229 --> 01:22:26.608
and things to do is 100 miles,

01:22:26.608 --> 01:22:29.152
but you cannot start your running career

01:22:29.152 --> 01:22:34.157
with 10K and one year later at
the start line of 100 miles.

01:22:34.741 --> 01:22:36.493
Yes, you can do it,

01:22:36.493 --> 01:22:38.203
and maybe you can finish it,

01:22:38.203 --> 01:22:40.455
but if you think longevity,

01:22:40.455 --> 01:22:41.831
if you think progression,

01:22:41.831 --> 01:22:46.628
how you can sprint from 10K
to 100 miles in one year.

01:22:47.963 --> 01:22:51.007
Yes, if you take a look at that,

01:22:51.007 --> 01:22:53.677
if you have a look on that,
it's not just possible.

01:22:53.677 --> 01:22:56.179
So I think the progression
is really, really important,

01:22:56.179 --> 01:22:59.474
and to think that yes,
you have time to do it

01:22:59.474 --> 01:23:02.894
because for me, 100 miles is the dream.

01:23:02.894 --> 01:23:06.398
So if you achieve your dream too fast,

01:23:06.398 --> 01:23:08.942
then okay, you can have some other dream.

01:23:08.942 --> 01:23:11.194
But if it's a big dream,

01:23:11.194 --> 01:23:13.905
no matter if it take you one
year, or two year, three year,

01:23:13.905 --> 01:23:15.615
five years maybe

01:23:15.615 --> 01:23:19.369
it's maybe a better dream
if it take long time

01:23:19.369 --> 01:23:20.537
to achieve it in.

01:23:20.537 --> 01:23:23.164
So I think it's very important

01:23:23.164 --> 01:23:24.916
to have this kind of progression,

01:23:24.916 --> 01:23:26.001
to have different test,

01:23:26.001 --> 01:23:27.127
to have different history,

01:23:27.127 --> 01:23:28.753
to take time to meet the people,

01:23:28.753 --> 01:23:31.256
to discover yourself, to test.

01:23:32.424 --> 01:23:34.884
Yeah, I, we have, my partner,

01:23:34.884 --> 01:23:37.429
we work since 10 years
to develop the product

01:23:37.429 --> 01:23:38.805
and to test the product.

01:23:38.805 --> 01:23:42.726
So it's so interesting to test
these kind of bags of shoes.

01:23:42.726 --> 01:23:45.145
What is better for us,

01:23:45.145 --> 01:23:47.480
and the nutrition
strategy, and everything,

01:23:47.480 --> 01:23:49.482
I think it's so interesting
to test everything,

01:23:49.482 --> 01:23:52.777
so people have to take
time to test everything,

01:23:52.777 --> 01:23:54.154
to test themselves,

01:23:54.154 --> 01:23:57.699
to discover themselves before
going to the 100 miles,

01:23:57.699 --> 01:24:01.661
but the second thing that
you say is true, that's, wow,

01:24:01.661 --> 01:24:02.495
100 miles.

01:24:02.495 --> 01:24:04.998
It looks like impossible, but not.

01:24:04.998 --> 01:24:08.585
I think 100 miles is even
more possible than a marathon,

01:24:08.585 --> 01:24:11.796
because in marathon you have
the perspective of performance

01:24:11.796 --> 01:24:13.089
enough time.

01:24:13.089 --> 01:24:15.800
And maybe New York Marathon
it's a bit different

01:24:15.800 --> 01:24:16.634
because it's, okay,

01:24:16.634 --> 01:24:19.179
I just want to do New York
Marathon no matter the time.

01:24:19.179 --> 01:24:21.222
But normally people in marathon,

01:24:21.222 --> 01:24:22.348
running marathons,

01:24:22.348 --> 01:24:24.059
they want to put time.

01:24:24.059 --> 01:24:26.478
On one on one, no one tell of time.

01:24:26.478 --> 01:24:28.438
You just want to finish it.

01:24:28.438 --> 01:24:30.648
For the first one that
was the last runner.

01:24:30.648 --> 01:24:31.483
It's the same goal,

01:24:31.483 --> 01:24:34.319
it's just to achieve this
adventure and this journey.

01:24:34.319 --> 01:24:37.989
And it's so hard and so interesting to do.

01:24:37.989 --> 01:24:40.158
But it's not impossible,

01:24:40.158 --> 01:24:42.494
because it could be just walking,

01:24:42.494 --> 01:24:43.745
just running.

01:24:43.745 --> 01:24:47.957
And if you go it slowly,
I'm sure it's possible,

01:24:47.957 --> 01:24:50.794
but you have to be really
passionate about that

01:24:50.794 --> 01:24:53.296
and you have to know why you do that.

01:24:53.296 --> 01:24:55.965
If you are at the start
line of one 100 mile race,

01:24:55.965 --> 01:24:57.759
just because it's a bet with your friend,

01:24:57.759 --> 01:25:00.762
or just because you dream-
- You're in trouble.

01:25:00.762 --> 01:25:02.222
- And you say, okay,

01:25:02.222 --> 01:25:04.349
I made this bet with my
friend and now I'm here,

01:25:04.349 --> 01:25:06.518
but I'm not sure I want to be there.

01:25:06.518 --> 01:25:08.019
Okay, don't take the start

01:25:08.019 --> 01:25:10.396
because running 100 mile

01:25:10.396 --> 01:25:13.900
it must be something that
you feel in your heart,

01:25:13.900 --> 01:25:16.694
and you are really motivated about that

01:25:16.694 --> 01:25:18.363
because of course it'll be hard,

01:25:18.363 --> 01:25:20.532
but if you know why you are here,

01:25:20.532 --> 01:25:22.117
if it's a dream,

01:25:22.117 --> 01:25:23.618
I'm sure it's possible to do.

01:25:23.618 --> 01:25:24.452
- Hmm, yeah.

01:25:24.452 --> 01:25:28.373
Knowing your why and patience, right?

01:25:28.373 --> 01:25:31.334
That idea of progression
really is about patience.

01:25:31.334 --> 01:25:34.754
I think so many people really overestimate

01:25:34.754 --> 01:25:36.089
what they can do in a year,

01:25:36.089 --> 01:25:37.841
and they bite off more than they can chew

01:25:37.841 --> 01:25:39.425
and then find out quickly enough

01:25:39.425 --> 01:25:41.636
that maybe that wasn't possible.

01:25:41.636 --> 01:25:43.054
And then they give up,

01:25:43.054 --> 01:25:44.973
and they miss the greater opportunity,

01:25:44.973 --> 01:25:48.726
which is understanding what's
possible with persistence

01:25:48.726 --> 01:25:51.020
and patience over an
extended period of time.

01:25:51.020 --> 01:25:52.480
Maybe it's 10 years, but-

01:25:52.480 --> 01:25:54.232
- Yeah, even for me.

01:25:54.232 --> 01:25:57.068
- Something you slowly,
slowly iterate on it

01:25:57.068 --> 01:25:58.820
in that really non-sexy way

01:25:58.820 --> 01:26:01.030
that no one's paying attention to,

01:26:01.030 --> 01:26:04.325
that's truly how you
accomplish these goals

01:26:04.325 --> 01:26:05.952
that seem audacious.

01:26:05.952 --> 01:26:08.246
- Yeah, I think I start
running long distance

01:26:08.246 --> 01:26:10.415
in just, yes.

01:26:10.415 --> 01:26:11.499
- I mean,

01:26:11.499 --> 01:26:13.877
were you a guy who won your
first races right out of the bat

01:26:13.877 --> 01:26:15.753
and were just winning
everything that you entered?

01:26:15.753 --> 01:26:17.589
- No, no, no, no.

01:26:17.589 --> 01:26:18.673
It's even for me,

01:26:18.673 --> 01:26:21.301
and I was able to win some big ultra race,

01:26:21.301 --> 01:26:24.888
it's taken me 10 years to do it.

01:26:24.888 --> 01:26:27.098
So 10 years is not nothing.

01:26:27.098 --> 01:26:30.643
So I'm sure I can do it in 4, 5, 6 years,

01:26:30.643 --> 01:26:33.271
but yes,

01:26:33.271 --> 01:26:35.815
4, 5, 6 years for people it's too long,

01:26:36.941 --> 01:26:41.946
but I think it's not a big
deal to make the 100 mile race,

01:26:42.322 --> 01:26:43.156
is not nothing.

01:26:43.156 --> 01:26:45.074
And if you consider it like, oh, okay,

01:26:45.074 --> 01:26:47.744
it's just 100 mile race,

01:26:47.744 --> 01:26:49.245
you say I can do it,

01:26:49.245 --> 01:26:51.289
so I will do it in one year.

01:26:51.289 --> 01:26:53.791
No, I think it's not the
good approach 100 mile race.

01:26:53.791 --> 01:26:54.876
It's not nothing.

01:26:54.876 --> 01:26:57.045
And if you think it's nothing,

01:26:57.045 --> 01:26:58.087
it'll be too hard for you.

01:26:58.087 --> 01:27:00.506
- Right.
(man laughing)

01:27:01.591 --> 01:27:03.301
That's a very wise thing to say.

01:27:03.301 --> 01:27:04.135
Yeah,

01:27:04.135 --> 01:27:05.762
I mean how about just start with,

01:27:05.762 --> 01:27:08.681
can you go out and walk
around a mountain all day,

01:27:08.681 --> 01:27:10.391
you know, like instead of thinking about

01:27:10.391 --> 01:27:11.517
how fast you can run,

01:27:11.517 --> 01:27:14.062
and how long you can
sustain a certain pace.

01:27:14.938 --> 01:27:17.774
- Yeah, I think it's a
best thing say just to say,

01:27:17.774 --> 01:27:21.486
okay, no matter the pace,

01:27:21.486 --> 01:27:22.779
no matter the elevation,

01:27:22.779 --> 01:27:27.325
no matter the distance and
everybody say about training,

01:27:27.325 --> 01:27:28.576
what is your mileage?

01:27:28.576 --> 01:27:30.536
What is the distance you do each week?

01:27:30.536 --> 01:27:32.538
I say, I don't know.
(man chuckling)

01:27:32.538 --> 01:27:35.291
Even for my event that we
will create in September,

01:27:35.291 --> 01:27:36.918
we don't want to give the distance.

01:27:36.918 --> 01:27:37.919
We will say to people,

01:27:37.919 --> 01:27:41.798
okay, you will have to spend
five to six hours in mountain.

01:27:41.798 --> 01:27:43.591
Yeah, but what is the distance?

01:27:43.591 --> 01:27:45.093
I don't know.

01:27:45.093 --> 01:27:46.177
(man laughing)

01:27:46.177 --> 01:27:47.011
I don't know.

01:27:47.011 --> 01:27:48.054
It's,

01:27:48.054 --> 01:27:49.055
maybe I can give you elevation gain,

01:27:49.055 --> 01:27:51.808
maybe I can say you some
different thing, but I don't know.

01:27:51.808 --> 01:27:53.226
It will depend your pace,

01:27:53.226 --> 01:27:54.936
it will depend the forecast,

01:27:54.936 --> 01:27:57.855
it will depend some terrain, everything.

01:27:57.855 --> 01:27:59.440
But I don't know what
would be the distance.

01:27:59.440 --> 01:28:02.235
It's just you have to be able to spend

01:28:02.235 --> 01:28:03.945
like six hours the first day

01:28:03.945 --> 01:28:06.197
and eleven hours the
second day in the mountain,

01:28:06.197 --> 01:28:10.076
and then we would see what
would be the distance.

01:28:10.076 --> 01:28:11.327
- [Rich] Right.
- We don't know,

01:28:11.327 --> 01:28:12.787
and I don't want to know.

01:28:12.787 --> 01:28:14.664
- That'll drive Americans crazy.

01:28:14.664 --> 01:28:17.000
But what's great about that
is it forces you to let go

01:28:17.000 --> 01:28:19.961
of all of those attachments
and expectations.

01:28:19.961 --> 01:28:24.966
Like, can you free yourself
from what you imagine it is,

01:28:25.466 --> 01:28:27.302
or it can or will be,

01:28:27.302 --> 01:28:30.096
and just be in the experience,

01:28:30.096 --> 01:28:32.515
which is really what it's about, right?

01:28:32.515 --> 01:28:33.558
- Yeah, yeah.

01:28:33.558 --> 01:28:34.976
No, it's a good way.

01:28:36.102 --> 01:28:36.936
- Where do you,

01:28:37.937 --> 01:28:39.022
what do you,

01:28:39.022 --> 01:28:42.900
you have your idea of what you
want to do with these races

01:28:42.900 --> 01:28:43.901
that you're creating,

01:28:43.901 --> 01:28:47.947
but where do you see the
future of trail running

01:28:47.947 --> 01:28:50.408
and ultra running like 10 years from now?

01:28:50.408 --> 01:28:52.535
You know, how are you thinking about

01:28:52.535 --> 01:28:54.662
the new generation of young, ultra runners

01:28:54.662 --> 01:28:55.580
who are coming up

01:28:55.580 --> 01:28:57.957
and what is that world gonna look like

01:28:57.957 --> 01:28:59.625
in the not too distant future?

01:29:01.085 --> 01:29:02.420
- It's hard to say

01:29:02.420 --> 01:29:05.798
because I'm so happy that
there's more, and more, and more

01:29:05.798 --> 01:29:07.884
people practicing trail running,

01:29:07.884 --> 01:29:10.845
but in a sustainable way.

01:29:10.845 --> 01:29:12.221
You can say, okay,

01:29:12.221 --> 01:29:14.057
it's more and more event,

01:29:14.057 --> 01:29:16.351
and more and more thing organized,

01:29:16.351 --> 01:29:20.188
and if you start a race
now you are 100 people

01:29:20.188 --> 01:29:23.107
and in 10 years you are 10,000 people.

01:29:23.107 --> 01:29:24.859
I think it's too much for the track,

01:29:24.859 --> 01:29:26.903
it's too much for everything,

01:29:26.903 --> 01:29:28.488
so that's why with the event,

01:29:28.488 --> 01:29:31.657
and that's why I think with
the organizer and runner,

01:29:31.657 --> 01:29:35.953
we say okay, two race
in a year, it's good.

01:29:35.953 --> 01:29:37.747
I think it's good for the body

01:29:37.747 --> 01:29:39.707
and it's good for the planet too,

01:29:39.707 --> 01:29:43.086
because I can do like
10 trail run in a year,

01:29:43.086 --> 01:29:45.797
but it's mean that 10 travel.

01:29:45.797 --> 01:29:49.008
If you do only two,
it's already two travel.

01:29:49.008 --> 01:29:49.842
Okay, it's a lot.

01:29:49.842 --> 01:29:52.637
But it's only two travel for
international, national outlet.

01:29:52.637 --> 01:29:55.598
I think it's a minimum that I have to do

01:29:55.598 --> 01:29:57.975
to meet the community and to be there

01:29:59.143 --> 01:30:01.604
at the top of the international race.

01:30:01.604 --> 01:30:03.064
But it's only two races.

01:30:03.064 --> 01:30:05.900
And that's why I try
to discuss with people

01:30:05.900 --> 01:30:06.818
that there's only,

01:30:08.152 --> 01:30:11.447
there's not only a life
when you have a big number.

01:30:11.447 --> 01:30:13.366
You can make things by yourself.

01:30:13.366 --> 01:30:14.617
And that's why in my heaven,

01:30:14.617 --> 01:30:16.369
and that's why when I discuss with you

01:30:16.369 --> 01:30:17.203
and something like that,

01:30:17.203 --> 01:30:21.416
I say a lot that you have
to experience yourself alone

01:30:21.416 --> 01:30:23.501
in the mountain to discover yourself,

01:30:23.501 --> 01:30:26.712
to understand how,

01:30:26.712 --> 01:30:28.214
when you go in the mountain,

01:30:28.214 --> 01:30:30.216
you have to take care of the forecast,

01:30:30.216 --> 01:30:31.426
of your equipment,

01:30:31.426 --> 01:30:32.260
about the map,

01:30:32.260 --> 01:30:33.261
about everything,

01:30:33.261 --> 01:30:34.929
and you have to take a headlamp,

01:30:34.929 --> 01:30:36.556
you have to take a survival blanket,

01:30:36.556 --> 01:30:40.977
and you have to, yes, to
take care from each other

01:30:40.977 --> 01:30:41.936
if you are in a group.

01:30:41.936 --> 01:30:43.479
And I think it's very important.

01:30:43.479 --> 01:30:45.064
And I think in 10 years,

01:30:46.357 --> 01:30:48.818
I'm sure that there will
be more, and more, and more

01:30:48.818 --> 01:30:49.652
trail runner,

01:30:49.652 --> 01:30:53.322
but maybe less races,

01:30:53.322 --> 01:30:56.409
and maybe people they
will do it by themselves,

01:30:56.409 --> 01:31:00.037
and they will organize
their adventure by themself,

01:31:00.037 --> 01:31:01.581
and with that,

01:31:01.581 --> 01:31:05.793
there's ton of possibility and no limit

01:31:05.793 --> 01:31:09.881
because you can imagine
your personal adventure

01:31:09.881 --> 01:31:12.133
and what is more relevant for you.

01:31:12.133 --> 01:31:14.802
And because may I say that my season

01:31:14.802 --> 01:31:17.305
is from July to October,

01:31:17.305 --> 01:31:21.017
but every place on the world are different

01:31:21.017 --> 01:31:22.268
and every people are different,

01:31:22.268 --> 01:31:25.229
so there's no definition of trail running

01:31:25.229 --> 01:31:28.774
because you can do it along the coast,

01:31:28.774 --> 01:31:30.193
you can do it in the mountain,

01:31:30.193 --> 01:31:31.861
you can do it in the middle of-

01:31:31.861 --> 01:31:33.738
- It's whatever you decide it to be.

01:31:33.738 --> 01:31:34.572
- Yeah.

01:31:34.572 --> 01:31:36.199
And me, I like when it's in the mountain,

01:31:36.199 --> 01:31:39.160
but for some people they prefer
to do it in a single trail,

01:31:39.160 --> 01:31:40.495
flat above the ocean.

01:31:40.495 --> 01:31:41.954
And everybody's different

01:31:41.954 --> 01:31:44.081
and everybody have some different tastes

01:31:44.081 --> 01:31:46.626
or with that evolution,

01:31:46.626 --> 01:31:50.922
everybody can build their own
adventure by themself alone,

01:31:50.922 --> 01:31:52.381
long distance, short distance,

01:31:52.381 --> 01:31:54.133
coast distance, mountain coast,

01:31:54.133 --> 01:31:55.551
challenge.

01:31:55.551 --> 01:31:58.387
And what is important
for me is that people,

01:31:58.387 --> 01:31:59.805
they can discover themselves,

01:31:59.805 --> 01:32:01.349
they can discover the natural,

01:32:01.349 --> 01:32:05.770
and they're out from some
long day in the mountain

01:32:05.770 --> 01:32:06.854
and people say,

01:32:06.854 --> 01:32:09.023
yeah, it's not sustainable traveling,

01:32:09.023 --> 01:32:10.358
and too many race, too many event.

01:32:10.358 --> 01:32:12.944
Yeah, but you can just practice running

01:32:12.944 --> 01:32:13.903
without any race,

01:32:13.903 --> 01:32:17.281
without any event, and by yourself.

01:32:17.281 --> 01:32:20.576
And I think it's a good approach.

01:32:20.576 --> 01:32:23.746
I would like to say to people,

01:32:23.746 --> 01:32:24.580
try it,

01:32:24.580 --> 01:32:25.414
test it,

01:32:25.414 --> 01:32:26.249
play with that.

01:32:26.249 --> 01:32:30.419
And for me it's so passionate
since more than 20 years,

01:32:30.419 --> 01:32:34.590
and so I'd like to push people to say,

01:32:34.590 --> 01:32:38.177
okay, try it and you would
see it's possible to do thing

01:32:38.177 --> 01:32:41.097
that you are not thinking it's possible.

01:32:41.097 --> 01:32:43.474
It's just 20 years ago,

01:32:43.474 --> 01:32:46.811
for me doing like, Hardrock 100,

01:32:46.811 --> 01:32:48.646
it's just unbelievable, right?

01:32:48.646 --> 01:32:50.022
And 20 years later,

01:32:50.022 --> 01:32:53.025
I was able to want it and to
have the record on that race,

01:32:53.025 --> 01:32:54.485
so nothing is impossible.

01:32:54.485 --> 01:32:56.195
So you can do it.

01:32:56.195 --> 01:32:59.949
And the victory is not just about winning,

01:32:59.949 --> 01:33:02.577
it's just accomplish your dream.

01:33:02.577 --> 01:33:06.622
So this is what is
interesting in trail running

01:33:06.622 --> 01:33:07.456
and ultra distance

01:33:07.456 --> 01:33:10.126
is that everybody has his own victory

01:33:10.126 --> 01:33:12.128
and everybody can share the same dream

01:33:12.128 --> 01:33:13.296
and the same adventure,

01:33:13.296 --> 01:33:16.424
because when we are on the start line

01:33:16.424 --> 01:33:18.843
of the Hardrock 100,

01:33:18.843 --> 01:33:20.094
the winner of the race,

01:33:20.094 --> 01:33:23.848
since the last winner of
the race has the same dream,

01:33:23.848 --> 01:33:26.767
it's just to finish the loop,

01:33:26.767 --> 01:33:28.769
and to see the mountain again.

01:33:28.769 --> 01:33:30.479
No matter the place,

01:33:30.479 --> 01:33:33.608
we just want to finish
it and to accomplish it.

01:33:33.608 --> 01:33:38.362
And I think this is unique
in all of the other sport.

01:33:38.362 --> 01:33:39.614
- Yeah, yeah.

01:33:39.614 --> 01:33:41.616
That's really, that's beautifully put.

01:33:41.616 --> 01:33:46.287
I mean there is this
inherent sort of paradox

01:33:46.287 --> 01:33:48.372
with the growth of trail running,

01:33:48.372 --> 01:33:49.540
because the roots of it,

01:33:49.540 --> 01:33:51.959
and what is so alluring about it

01:33:51.959 --> 01:33:53.961
is that connection with nature,

01:33:53.961 --> 01:33:57.757
and that kind of the solitude of it all,

01:33:57.757 --> 01:34:00.426
and the, you know, the kind of silence,

01:34:00.426 --> 01:34:03.638
just you and your breath,
and the wind, and whatnot.

01:34:03.638 --> 01:34:06.641
But as these races and
interest in this world

01:34:06.641 --> 01:34:07.683
continue to grow,

01:34:07.683 --> 01:34:10.686
suddenly these, you know,
you're sleeping in a tent

01:34:10.686 --> 01:34:12.605
at the starting line and
there's two people there,

01:34:12.605 --> 01:34:13.439
whatever.

01:34:13.439 --> 01:34:15.358
Now there's, you know, media,

01:34:15.358 --> 01:34:16.400
and it's money,

01:34:16.400 --> 01:34:19.153
and all the commercialization
and all of that,

01:34:19.153 --> 01:34:21.656
which obviously is antithetical

01:34:21.656 --> 01:34:23.532
to the whole spirit of the entire thing.

01:34:23.532 --> 01:34:27.703
But I think what is great about
these self-styled adventures

01:34:27.703 --> 01:34:30.247
is that that's where
people's heads are at, right?

01:34:30.247 --> 01:34:32.333
I mean, the pandemic,
when all the races ended,

01:34:32.333 --> 01:34:34.085
everybody had to get creative

01:34:34.085 --> 01:34:36.671
and suddenly you saw
this explosion of people

01:34:36.671 --> 01:34:38.964
just saying, well, I don't
need to wait for permission

01:34:38.964 --> 01:34:40.007
for this race to happen.

01:34:40.007 --> 01:34:42.426
I'm gonna go out and like do my own thing.

01:34:42.426 --> 01:34:44.470
And now I feel like
there's a lot of momentum

01:34:44.470 --> 01:34:47.431
behind that type of endeavor.

01:34:47.431 --> 01:34:49.225
And it doesn't have to be an FKT.

01:34:49.225 --> 01:34:53.521
It could just be, hey, I have
a trail a mile from my house

01:34:53.521 --> 01:34:54.980
that I've never gone on before.

01:34:54.980 --> 01:34:56.273
Let's see what we can do.

01:34:56.273 --> 01:34:57.608
Let's have some fun.

01:34:57.608 --> 01:34:59.235
- First time is a thing,

01:34:59.235 --> 01:35:01.028
but a trail is a thing too.

01:35:01.028 --> 01:35:02.863
And just trying to do something

01:35:02.863 --> 01:35:04.949
is I think something very good.

01:35:04.949 --> 01:35:07.952
And even for me, when I start FKT,

01:35:10.204 --> 01:35:12.164
okay, so FKT team must be a good excuse

01:35:12.164 --> 01:35:14.083
with all the partner and everything,

01:35:15.334 --> 01:35:16.627
and for my feelings,

01:35:16.627 --> 01:35:18.546
the best thing is just to try it,

01:35:18.546 --> 01:35:19.422
and to do it.

01:35:19.422 --> 01:35:21.549
And okay, the race is crowded.

01:35:21.549 --> 01:35:25.553
Many people, it's too much sometimes,

01:35:25.553 --> 01:35:27.471
but it's, if I did two race,

01:35:27.471 --> 01:35:31.308
it's 40 hour and it's 800 hour
of training for 40 hour also.

01:35:31.308 --> 01:35:32.643
It's not a lot.
- Right.

01:35:32.643 --> 01:35:33.936
(men laughing)

01:35:33.936 --> 01:35:34.770
Right.

01:35:36.230 --> 01:35:37.189
Fantastic, man.

01:35:37.189 --> 01:35:39.608
Well I think that's a good place

01:35:39.608 --> 01:35:42.445
to kind of end it for today.

01:35:42.445 --> 01:35:45.489
I'm excited to watch you race at Hardrock.

01:35:45.489 --> 01:35:47.324
Seems like you're in good spirits

01:35:47.324 --> 01:35:49.118
and your body is cooperating,

01:35:49.118 --> 01:35:52.747
so I think it's gonna be
exciting to watch that show down.

01:35:52.747 --> 01:35:53.581
- Yeah, yeah.

01:35:53.581 --> 01:35:57.293
It will be so nice anyway what's happened.

01:35:57.293 --> 01:35:58.210
We will see.

01:35:58.210 --> 01:36:02.256
And no matter I'm just happy to be there,

01:36:02.256 --> 01:36:03.466
and to come back there,

01:36:03.466 --> 01:36:06.969
and for me it was a good
moment to share with you

01:36:06.969 --> 01:36:10.306
at least then I'm so happy
to make this experience,

01:36:10.306 --> 01:36:14.769
and I'm sure I would have some memories

01:36:14.769 --> 01:36:16.687
from the next adventure.

01:36:16.687 --> 01:36:17.521
- Yeah.

01:36:17.521 --> 01:36:18.439
Very cool.

01:36:18.439 --> 01:36:20.149
Well, let's continue this
conversation at a later date.

01:36:20.149 --> 01:36:21.859
I'd love to have you back on,

01:36:21.859 --> 01:36:25.613
and I really appreciate you
bringing all your thoughtfulness

01:36:25.613 --> 01:36:28.282
and experience to this conversation.

01:36:28.282 --> 01:36:29.116
It's really cool.

01:36:29.116 --> 01:36:32.495
So what you're doing is really inspiring.

01:36:32.495 --> 01:36:36.457
I think it really inspires all of us

01:36:36.457 --> 01:36:39.460
to kind of reach a little
bit further and deeper,

01:36:39.460 --> 01:36:40.753
and, you know, kind of what you said

01:36:40.753 --> 01:36:43.005
about how it took you 20
years to get where you're at.

01:36:43.005 --> 01:36:45.716
It's very easy to look at
someone like yourself and say,

01:36:45.716 --> 01:36:47.802
well, it's easy for him.

01:36:47.802 --> 01:36:50.471
He's built for this and all of that.

01:36:50.471 --> 01:36:51.972
And maybe there's some truth in that.

01:36:51.972 --> 01:36:52.807
But you know,

01:36:52.807 --> 01:36:55.684
to understand like the passion
that you have for the sport,

01:36:55.684 --> 01:36:56.519
the dedication,

01:36:56.519 --> 01:36:59.688
and just the love of the outdoors,

01:36:59.688 --> 01:37:02.024
and the joyful expression

01:37:02.024 --> 01:37:04.193
that you bring to everything that you do,

01:37:04.193 --> 01:37:07.488
I think is uplifting
for everybody to hear.

01:37:07.488 --> 01:37:09.532
So thank you for that.

01:37:09.532 --> 01:37:10.616
- Thank you very much.
- Cool.

